"text": "Keys are read from the environment. A .env file is read only if you load it, with vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") ; or pass keys in code: OpenAI(api_key=...) , Supabase(url=..., key=...) . Variable Read by OPENAI_API_KEY OpenAI , OpenAIEmbedder (also accepted as OPENAI_API ) ANTHROPIC_API_KEY Anthropic HF_TOKEN the first download of pyannote's gated speaker model; not needed once cached SUPABASE_URL , SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY , SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY Supabase : writes use the secret key, searches the publishable one VIDRA_DATA where output goes (default data/ in the checkout, else ~/.vidra ) VIDRA_WEIGHTS where checkpoints are cached (default weights/ ) .env.example lists them all."
