{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "Two tiers",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#tiers",
"text": "video_rag reads the video: eight stages, each reading files and writing one, ending with every chunk described and embedded. It also does search. aggregates reads only the files video_rag wrote, never the video, and answers questions about the whole: counts, summaries, chapters, people. workflow runs both in one call ( The pipeline )."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "The chunk grid",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#grid",
"text": "A video is cut into chunks : consecutive spans, typically 5 to 30 seconds, stored in timeline.json . Everything after is keyed by chunk_id : frames, transcript, descriptions, vectors. Chunk 7 is the same seconds in every file, and a search result is a chunk. The policy decides where boundaries fall: Policy Cuts at Needs uniform every chunk_s seconds (default 20) nothing scene cuts in the picture a scene-detection pass vad pauses in speech the transcript speaker changes of speaker the transcript, with speakers Chunks are kept between min_s and max_s : short ones merge, long ones split evenly, and a short last chunk joins the one before ( boundaries )."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "The video's folder",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#folder",
"text": "Each video gets <into>/<video_id>/ , with one file per stage: File Written by Holds media.json media container, streams, duration, a fingerprint of the file transcript.raw.json audio words and segments with times and speakers, before chunking cuts.json boundaries.evidence where the content changes, and the per-frame scores timeline.json boundaries the chunk grid manifest.json video per chunk, the frames each sampler kept store/ video the kept frames, as JPEGs transcript.json cut the transcript per chunk descriptions.json describe per chunk, one answer per sampler and question embedded.json embed every answer and transcript chunk as text, with its vector aggregates/ aggregates one file per whole-video answer (any folder you name) Fields: Reference ."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "Video ids",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#video-id",
"text": "The id is the folder name: the filename stem ( shop.mp4 is shop ) unless you pass video_id= . Allowed: ASCII letters, digits, - , _ , . , not starting with _ . A file like My Video!.mp4 needs an explicit video_id= . The same file again reuses its folder. A different file with the same id gets a new one ( shop-2 ), unless on_conflict is \"replace\" (deletes the old folder) or \"refuse\" (raises). Read the id from run.video_id ."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "Frames, samplers and questions",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#frames",
"text": "The video is decoded once and frames are offered at per_second (default 1). A sampler picks which to keep: every Nth ( uniform ), or when the scene, people, objects or on-screen text change ( clip , yolo , objects , text ). Samplers . A question is what the vision model is asked about those frames, and the fields its answer fills. Each sampler has its own; any sampler pairs with any question as sampler:question . Questions ."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "Answer ids",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#answer-ids",
"text": "Each answer is stored under an answer id , the sampler and the question: Sampler spec Answer ids clip clip (its own question) uniform:text uniform:text clip:[text,scene] clip:text , clip:scene , from one pass clip,clip:checkout clip , clip:checkout , from one pass A chunk's transcript has the id transcript . Search filters and aggregate inputs use these ids."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "Units and vector spaces",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#units",
"text": "A unit is one piece of embedded text: one answer for one chunk (its prose plus its fields), or one chunk's transcript. embedded.json holds every unit and its vector. Each vector is tagged with its embedder's key, e.g. local:BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5:384 . Vectors under different keys are never compared: search with the embedder that built the index ."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "Reuse",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#reuse",
"text": "Expensive work is reused when nothing it depends on changed: A description : same frames, same vision model and settings, same question wording. Editing one question re-describes only its answers. A vector : same text, same embedder key. An aggregate answer : same text read, same definition, same model key. The pipelines do this automatically. Stages and aggregators called directly take previous= , the earlier output (usually the file being overwritten)."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "Model keys",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#keys",
"text": "Every model has a key , e.g. openai:gpt-5.4-mini , stored with each answer and vector and compared for reuse. In your own model class, change the key when the model changes , or old answers are reused as the new model's. Models ."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "Files first, database second",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#files-first",
"text": "Every stage writes a file. With a database , the pipeline also sends each new document to it. A failed database write goes into run.problems and the run continues; the files are complete either way. Search reads from a database. Folder reads the output folder in place, so search works without a server. Databases ."
},
{
"page": "Concepts",
"title": "Errors",
"url": "pages/concepts.html#errors",
"text": "Everything raised on purpose is a vidra.VidraError . Two branches worth catching: vidra.Unavailable : something is missing (a package, weights, a key, a server). Retrying won't help. Refused : the request is invalid, e.g. min_s above max_s . Also a ValueError . Most problems are caught before work starts: unknown questions, settings no sampler reads, missing keys. Full list: Reference ."
},
{
"page": "Recipes",
"title": "Recipes",
"url": "pages/recipes.html",
"text": "Complete scripts, in docs/pages/examples/ . Recipe Shows Needs hosted.py OpenAI, a local embedder and Supabase: index, search, whole-video answers [all] , OpenAI and Supabase keys stage_by_stage.py every stage called on its own, with its settings [all] , an OpenAI key custom_question.py your own question, and searching by its fields [local] , an OpenAI key aggregates_tour.py every aggregator, one at a time and all at once [local] , an OpenAI key, a folder from hosted.py custom_aggregate.py custom prompts and a linking profile [local] , an OpenAI key, a video folder several_videos.py searching several videos and answering about them as one [all] , an OpenAI key custom_models.py your own VLM, LLM and embedder classes [local] , an OpenAI key custom_database.py your own database: SQLite, with search [all] , an OpenAI key Scripts read keys from .env in the folder you run them from, and write under data/ there. python docs/pages/examples/hosted.py samples/shop.mp4 python docs/pages/examples/aggregates_tour.py data/out/shop"
},
{
"page": "Recipes",
"title": "Hosted models, end to end",
"url": "pages/recipes.html#hosted",
"text": "OpenAI describes and summarises, a local embedder makes the vectors, Supabase keeps a copy and serves search. Use Folder(\"data/out\") instead of Supabase() to run without a server. docs/pages/examples/hosted.py \"\"\"The whole library with hosted models: OpenAI describes and summarises, a local embedder makes the vectors, Supabase keeps a copy and serves search. Needs: vidra[all], OPENAI_API_KEY, the Supabase variables (see Databases), and HF_TOKEN for pyannote's first download. python hosted.py path/to/video.mp4 \"\"\" import sys import vidra from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI, Supabase, aggregates from vidra.video_rag import search, video_rag vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") # keys from .env; nothing reads it otherwise source = sys.argv[1] models = Models( vlm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), # describes the frames llm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), # summary, chapters, events, entity accounts embedder=LocalEmbedder(), # BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5, on this machine ) database = Supabase() # or Folder(\"data/out\") for no server # Chunk at picture cuts; keep frames when the scene or the people change. run = video_rag(source, \"data/out\", policy=\"scene\", sampler=\"clip,yolo\", models=models, database=database) print(run.video_id, \"->\", run.folder) if run.problems: print(\"database writes that failed:\", run.problems) for query in (\"someone paying at the till\", \"a person in a red jacket\"): moments, notes = search(query, run.video_id, models=models, database=database) print(f\"\\n{query!r}\") for m in moments: best = m.hits[0] print(f\" {m.start_ts:6.1f}-{m.end_ts:6.1f}s {best['sampler_id']:<6} \" f\"{best['content'][:90]}\") # Whole-video answers: everything the run read, and who appears. d = run.folder video = aggregates.record(timeline=d / \"timeline.json\", transcript=d / \"transcript.json\", descriptions=d / \"descriptions.json\", manifest=d / \"manifest.json\") told = video.excerpt(transcript=True, answers={\"clip\": [\"summary\"], \"yolo\": [\"summary\"]}) done = aggregates.aggregate( out=d / \"aggregates\", previous=d / \"aggregates\", models=models, database=database, stats=video, summary=told, chapters=told, events=told, entities_people=video.sightings(profile=\"people\", answers=[\"yolo\"]), ) print(\"\\nskipped:\", done.stats[\"skipped\"]) summary = aggregates.load(done.artifacts[\"summary\"]).payload print(\"\\n\" + summary[\"summary\"]) for chapter in aggregates.load(done.artifacts[\"chapters\"]).payload[\"chapters\"]: print(f\" {chapter['start_ts']:6.1f}s {chapter['title']}\")"
},
{
"page": "Recipes",
"title": "Every stage on its own",
"url": "pages/recipes.html#stage-by-stage",
"text": "What video_rag() does, with its defaults spelled out: Whisper's model and language, the scene threshold (calibrated, then retuned without decoding), chunk lengths, two samplers in one decode, progress reporting. docs/pages/examples/stage_by_stage.py \"\"\"Every video_rag stage called on its own, with its settings. This is what `video_rag()` does, with the knobs it leaves at their defaults exposed. Each stage reads files and writes one; D is the video's folder. python stage_by_stage.py path/to/video.mp4 \"\"\" import sys from pathlib import Path import vidra from vidra import LocalEmbedder, OpenAI from vidra.video_rag import audio, boundaries, cut, describe, embed, media, video vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") source = sys.argv[1] # 1. media: what the file holds. Makes the video's folder. made = media.media(source, \"data/out\", on_conflict=\"new\") D = Path(made.stats[\"folder\"]) print(\"video id:\", made.video_id) # 2. audio: the whole soundtrack, transcribed and diarized. audio.audio(D / \"media.json\", D / \"transcript.raw.json\", transcriber=\"whisper\", model=\"small\", language=\"en\", diarizer=\"pyannote\", exclusive=True) # 3. boundaries.evidence: where the picture changes (scene scores per frame). boundaries.evidence(D / \"cuts.json\", \"scene\", media=D / \"media.json\", stride=5, threshold=27.0) # How many cuts other thresholds would give, from the cached scores. for row in boundaries.calibrate(D / \"cuts.json\"): print(f\"threshold {row['threshold']:>5}: {row['cuts']} cuts\") boundaries.retune(D / \"cuts.json\", D / \"cuts.json\", threshold=30.0) # 4. boundaries: the chunk grid, 10 to 40 seconds a chunk. boundaries.boundaries(D / \"media.json\", D / \"timeline.json\", policy=\"scene\", cuts=D / \"cuts.json\", min_s=10, max_s=40) print(\"chunks:\", len(boundaries.load(D / \"timeline.json\"))) # 5. video: which frames to keep. Two samplers in one decode: uniform keeps # every 5th frame (one per 5 s at per_second=1) and is asked to read the # screen; clip keeps a frame when the scene changes. video.video(D / \"media.json\", D / \"timeline.json\", D / \"manifest.json\", store=D / \"store\", sampler=\"uniform:text,clip\", per_second=1.0, every_n=5, threshold=0.95, max_per_chunk=6) # 6. cut: the transcript onto the grid. cut.cut(D / \"timeline.json\", D / \"transcript.raw.json\", D / \"transcript.json\") # 7. describe: one model call per (chunk, sampler, question). def progress(event): print(f\" describe {event.completed}/{event.total} ({event.skipped} reused)\") describe.describe(D / \"manifest.json\", D / \"timeline.json\", D / \"store\", D / \"descriptions.json\", previous=D / \"descriptions.json\", vlm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), max_output_tokens=2000, on_progress=progress) # 8. embed: every answer and every chunk's transcript, as vectors. embed.embed(D / \"embedded.json\", descriptions=D / \"descriptions.json\", transcript=D / \"transcript.json\", previous=D / \"embedded.json\", timeline=D / \"timeline.json\", embedder=LocalEmbedder()) # Read any result back, typed. said = describe.load(D / \"descriptions.json\") first = said.chunks[0][\"samplers\"] for answer_id, answer in first.items(): print(answer_id, \"->\", answer[\"description\"][:80])"
},
{
"page": "Recipes",
"title": "Every aggregator",
"url": "pages/recipes.html#aggregates-tour",
"text": "On a folder written with sampler=\"clip,yolo\" : each aggregator alone, then all together through aggregate() , which reuses what is still current. docs/pages/examples/aggregates_tour.py \"\"\"Every aggregator, on a folder video_rag wrote: one at a time, then all at once. Run hosted.py (or video_rag with sampler=\"clip,yolo\") first. python aggregates_tour.py data/out/<video_id> \"\"\" import sys from pathlib import Path import vidra from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI, aggregates vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") D = Path(sys.argv[1]) models = Models(llm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), embedder=LocalEmbedder()) out = D / \"answers\" # A record: the documents, named by path. Only the timeline is required. video = aggregates.record(timeline=D / \"timeline.json\", transcript=D / \"transcript.json\", descriptions=D / \"descriptions.json\", manifest=D / \"manifest.json\") print(\"answers in this record:\", video.answer_ids()) # Inputs, built from the record. Nothing is read unless named. said = video.excerpt(transcript=True) # what was said seen = video.excerpt(answers={\"clip\": [\"summary\"]}) # what was seen both = video.excerpt(transcript=True, answers={\"clip\": [\"summary\", \"actions\"]}) people = video.sightings(profile=\"people\", answers=[\"yolo\"]) # each person entry # free: count the record. aggregates.stats(record=video, out=out / \"stats.json\") aggregates.coverage(record=video, out=out / \"coverage.json\") # local: small models on this machine (vidra[local]). aggregates.ner(input=both, out=out / \"ner.json\", labels=[\"person\", \"product\"]) aggregates.sentiment(input=both, out=out / \"sentiment.json\") # llm: model calls. aggregates.summary(input=both, out=out / \"summary.json\", models=models) aggregates.chapters(input=both, out=out / \"chapters.json\", models=models, max_spans=5, min_span_s=30) aggregates.events(input=seen, out=out / \"events.json\", models=models) try: aggregates.entities(profile=\"people\", input=people, out=out / \"people.json\", models=models) except aggregates.Inapplicable as why: # e.g. nobody was described print(\"entities skipped:\", why) for name in (\"stats\", \"summary\", \"chapters\", \"people\"): if (out / f\"{name}.json\").exists(): payload = aggregates.load(out / f\"{name}.json\").payload print(f\"\\n{name}:\", {k: payload[k] for k in list(payload)[:3]}) # The same, as one pipeline: cheapest first, reusing what is still current. done = aggregates.aggregate( out=D / \"aggregates\", previous=D / \"aggregates\", models=models, stats=video, coverage=video, speakers=video, ner=both, summary=both, chapters=both, events=seen, sentiment={\"spoken\": said, \"seen\": seen}, # two answers, labelled entities_people=people, settings={\"ner\": {\"labels\": [\"person\"]}, \"chapters\": {\"max_spans\": 4}}, ) print(\"\\nwrote:\", sorted(done.artifacts)) print(\"computed:\", done.stats[\"computed\"], \" skipped:\", done.stats[\"skipped\"])"
},
{
"page": "Recipes",
"title": "Several videos",
"url": "pages/recipes.html#several-videos",
"text": "Index each video, search across all of them, then combine them into one record and summarise it. docs/pages/examples/several_videos.py \"\"\"Several videos: index each, search across all of them, and answer about them as one. python several_videos.py monday.mp4 tuesday.mp4 \"\"\" import sys import vidra from vidra import Folder, LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI, aggregates from vidra.video_rag import search, video_rag vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") models = Models(vlm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), llm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), embedder=LocalEmbedder()) database = Folder(\"data/out\") runs = [video_rag(path, \"data/out\", sampler=\"clip\", models=models, database=database) for path in sys.argv[1:]] ids = [run.video_id for run in runs] # Leave video_id out to search every video the database holds, or name some. moments, notes = search(\"a person carrying a box\", ids, moments=5, models=models, database=database) for m in moments: print(f\"{m.video_id:<12} chunk {m.chunk_id:>3} {m.start_ts:6.1f}-{m.end_ts:6.1f}s\") # One record per video, then laid end to end on one clock. records = [aggregates.record(timeline=run.folder / \"timeline.json\", transcript=run.folder / \"transcript.json\", descriptions=run.folder / \"descriptions.json\") for run in runs] together = aggregates.combine(records=records, out=\"data/out/combined\") aggregates.summary(input=together.excerpt(transcript=True, answers={\"clip\": [\"summary\"]}), out=\"data/out/combined/summary.json\", models=models) print(aggregates.load(\"data/out/combined/summary.json\").payload[\"summary\"])"
},
{
"page": "The pipeline",
"title": "The pipeline",
"url": "pages/pipeline.html",
"text": "video_rag() runs every stage on one video. workflow runs it, then the aggregators."
},
{
"page": "The pipeline",
"title": "video_rag()",
"url": "pages/pipeline.html#video-rag",
"text": "from vidra.video_rag import video_rag video_rag(source, into, video_id=None, on_conflict=\"new\", name=None, recorded_at=None, policy=\"uniform\", use_video=True, use_audio=True, sampler=\"uniform\", vlm=None, embedder=None, resume=True, database=None, on_step=None, models=None) -> Run from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI, Supabase from vidra.video_rag import video_rag models = Models(vlm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), embedder=LocalEmbedder()) run = video_rag(\"shop.mp4\", \"data/out\", policy=\"scene\", sampler=\"clip,yolo\", models=models, database=Supabase()) Argument Default Meaning source required The video file. into required Parent folder; output goes to into/<video_id>/ . video_id filename stem The folder name ( Video ids ). on_conflict \"new\" If a different file holds the id: \"new\" mints shop-2 , \"replace\" deletes the old folder, \"refuse\" raises media.VideoIdTaken . name the filename Display name, stored in media.json ; kept by later runs that omit it. recorded_at container tags Recording time, a datetime or ISO 8601 string; kept by later runs that omit it. policy \"uniform\" Where chunks are cut: uniform , scene , vad , speaker ( the grid ). use_video True Read the picture ( video and describe ). use_audio True Read the soundtrack ( audio and cut ). Needs vidra[audio] . sampler \"uniform\" Which frames to keep and what to ask, e.g. \"clip,yolo:overview\" ( specs ). vlm OpenAI() The vision model. Or set it in models . embedder OpenAIEmbedder() The embedder; search must use the same one. Or set it in models . resume True Reuse still-current descriptions and vectors. False redoes them. database none Where to copy every artifact: a Database , or \"supabase\" / \"folder\" . on_step none Progress callback ( below ). models none A Models with vlm and embedder . Giving a role here and as a keyword is refused. The policy, samplers, questions, model keys and database are all checked before the first stage; every problem is raised together as one Refused ."
},
{
"page": "The pipeline",
"title": "What it returns: Run",
"url": "pages/pipeline.html#run",
"text": "Attribute Is video_id The id used, which may differ from the one asked for. folder The video's folder, a Path . steps Each stage's receipt ( Produced ), in order: .component , .artifacts , .stats , .skipped . skipped {stage: why} for stages that did not run. problems Failed database writes. The files are still written. artifacts() {artifact: path} for every file in the folder. as_dict() The run as plain data. run.video_id # \"shop\" run.folder # Path(\"data/out/shop\") run.artifacts() # {\"descriptions\": \".../descriptions.json\", ...} run.skipped # {\"audio\": \"the file carries no audio stream\"} for step in run.steps: print(step.component, step.stats)"
},
{
"page": "The pipeline",
"title": "What runs, in what order",
"url": "pages/pipeline.html#order",
"text": "The policy decides the order: Policy Order uniform media, audio, boundaries, video, cut, describe, embed scene media, audio, boundaries.evidence (decodes the picture), boundaries, video, cut, describe, embed vad , speaker media, audio, boundaries.evidence (reads the transcript), boundaries, video, cut, describe, embed Stages that don't apply are skipped with a reason, e.g. audio on a silent file. A policy needing a stream the file lacks is refused. Each stage runs with its defaults: Whisper small and pyannote, scene threshold 27, chunks of 5 to 20 s, one frame per second. To change them, run the stages directly."
},
{
"page": "The pipeline",
"title": "Progress: on_step",
"url": "pages/pipeline.html#progress",
"text": "on_step(component, produced) is called before each stage (with None ) and after it (with its Produced ). With a third parameter it also gets a Progress for each unit of work in video , describe and embed : def on_step(component, produced, progress=None): if progress is not None: print(f\" {component} {progress.completed}/{progress.total} \" f\"({progress.skipped} reused) {progress.current}\") elif produced is None: print(\"start\", component) else: print(\"done \", component, produced.stats) video_rag(\"shop.mp4\", \"data/out\", sampler=\"clip\", on_step=on_step) Progress has component , total , completed , skipped , current (e.g. 3:clip ) and result . Describe reports in completion order. Raising in the callback stops the run."
},
{
"page": "The pipeline",
"title": "Options, process, validate",
"url": "pages/pipeline.html#options",
"text": "video_rag() is shorthand for these: from pathlib import Path from vidra.video_rag import Options, process, validate options = Options(source=Path(\"shop.mp4\"), into=Path(\"data/out\"), policy=\"scene\", sampler=\"clip\", vlm=OpenAI(), embedder=LocalEmbedder()) problems = validate(options) # [] when the request is valid; nothing runs if not problems: run = process(options, on_step=None) Options has video_rag() 's fields except on_step and models . validate(options) returns every problem as a list; process(options, on_step) runs it."
},
{
"page": "The pipeline",
"title": "layout()",
"url": "pages/pipeline.html#layout",
"text": "layout(folder) gives every artifact's path in a video's folder: from vidra.video_rag import layout at = layout(\"data/out/shop\") at[\"timeline\"] # Path(\"data/out/shop/timeline.json\") at[\"store\"] # Path(\"data/out/shop/store\")"
},
{
"page": "The pipeline",
"title": "workflow: both tiers",
"url": "pages/pipeline.html#workflow",
"text": "workflow.process runs video_rag , then every aggregator up to a cost tier . Answers go to <folder>/aggregates/ and are reused while current. from pathlib import Path from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI, Supabase, workflow run = workflow.process(workflow.Options( source=Path(\"shop.mp4\"), sampler=\"clip,yolo\", policy=\"scene\", tier=\"llm\", models=Models(vlm=OpenAI(), llm=OpenAI(), embedder=LocalEmbedder()), database=Supabase())) answers = run.steps[-1] # the aggregate step's receipt answers.artifacts # {\"summary\": \".../aggregates/summary.json\", ...} answers.stats[\"skipped\"] # {\"speakers\": \"...\", ...} workflow.Options(source, into=None, video_id=None, name=None, recorded_at=None, policy=\"uniform\", use_video=True, use_audio=True, sampler=\"uniform\", vlm=None, embedder=None, llm=None, tier=\"free\", database=None, models=None) video_rag() 's fields, plus: Field Default Meaning into the data root's out/ Optional here. llm OpenAI() The text model for the llm tier. Or set it in models . tier \"free\" The costliest tier to run: free , local or llm . Tier Runs Each reads free stats , coverage , speakers the record local the above, ner , sentiment the transcript and every answer's prose llm the above, summary , chapters , events , every custom prompt, and every linking profile ( entities:people , entities:objects , entities:text , custom ones) prompts: the transcript and every answer's prose; profiles: every answer An aggregator with nothing to read ( speakers on a silent video) is skipped with the reason. To choose inputs yourself, run the aggregates directly. workflow.validate(options) lists every problem either tier would raise, including a missing LLM key. workflow.process(options, on_step) reports \"aggregate\" as a final step. workflow.extraction(options) returns the video_rag.Options part. workflow.Run is a Run with the aggregate step last in steps ."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "Live streams",
"url": "pages/live.html",
"text": "Describe a stream while it plays: every frame a sampler keeps is answered as soon as it arrives, not when its chunk ends."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "Running one",
"url": "pages/live.html#basics",
"text": "from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI from vidra.video_rag import video_rag_live def check(o): # every answer, as it is ready if o.structured.get(\"rule\") == \"no_hard_hat\": print(f\"{o.seen_at} chunk {o.chunk_id} t={o.media_ts:.1f}s {o.description}\") run = video_rag_live(\"tcp://0.0.0.0:9000?listen=1\", \"data/out\", video_id=\"dock-3\", sampler=\"clip:safety\", on_unit=check, models=Models(vlm=OpenAI(), embedder=LocalEmbedder())) print(run.observations, \"answers,\", run.dropped, \"dropped, lag\", run.lag_s) The call blocks until the stream ends. Detection belongs in your on_unit : the pipeline describes and embeds, your application decides what counts as an event. An exact match on a one_of field ( fields ) is more reliable than comparing vectors: embeddings handle negation badly, so \"wearing a hard hat\" and \"without a hard hat\" sit close together."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "Testing with a file",
"url": "pages/live.html#testing",
"text": "live.send pushes a file to a port at the pace it was recorded. The receiver loads its samplers' models before it listens (about 20-35 s for clip , yolo and objects ), so the sender retries for up to connect_timeout_s . import multiprocessing from vidra.video_rag import live, video_rag_live if __name__ == \"__main__\": sender = multiprocessing.Process(target=live.send, args=(\"samples/test.mp4\", \"tcp://127.0.0.1:9000\"), kwargs={\"speed\": 1.0}) sender.start() run = video_rag_live(\"tcp://127.0.0.1:9000?listen=1\", \"data/out\", video_id=\"test-live\") sender.join() Run the sender in its own process, as a camera would be: while it waits to connect, PyAV holds the GIL, and on a thread of the same process it slows the receiver's model loading many times over. send(path, url, speed=1.0, connect_timeout_s=120.0, format=None) copies the picture without re-encoding, into MPEG-TS for H.264, HEVC and MPEG-2/4 and into Matroska for the rest (VP9, AV1); format= overrides. A codec this PyAV cannot write (Theora) is refused: re-encode it first. A file path is also a valid source : it is then read as fast as it decodes, which keeps exactly the frames video_rag keeps with the uniform policy. Sources are anything PyAV opens: tcp://host:port?listen=1 , udp:// , rtmp:// , an rtsp:// camera. The PyAV wheels have no SRT."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "Arguments",
"url": "pages/live.html#arguments",
"text": "video_rag_live(source, into, video_id=None, name=None, sampler=\"uniform\", vlm=None, embedder=None, database=None, on_unit=None, on_step=None, models=None, chunk_s=20.0, per_second=1.0, context=(0, 0), queue=64, record=False, stop_after_s=None, stop=None, open_timeout_s=60.0, read_timeout_s=10.0) -> LiveRun Argument Default Meaning source required A stream URL, or a file. into required The folder that holds one folder per video. video_id file stem, or live-<UTC time> The run's folder. A folder already in use gets -2 , -3 . name the id What to call the video in media.json . sampler \"uniform\" The same spec as video_rag ( samplers ). vlm , embedder , models OpenAI's The models, as in video_rag . database none Copy the documents here when the stream ends. on_unit none Called with each Observation . Raise live.StopStream to end the run. on_step none on_step(component, produced) : once when the stream opens, then per document written. chunk_s 20.0 Chunk length. A chunk is int(media_ts // chunk_s) : an id and a point where samplers reset. per_second 1.0 Decimated frames per second. context (0, 0) (before, after) : decimated frames sent with each kept frame ( below ). queue 64 Kept frames that may wait for the model; when full, the oldest is dropped. record False True keeps the stream as recording.ts in the run's folder; or a path. stop_after_s none Stop when the stream's clock reaches this. stop none A threading.Event ; set it from anywhere to end the run. open_timeout_s , read_timeout_s 60.0 , 10.0 How long to wait for a sender, and for the next packet. Everything is checked before the stream opens: an unknown sampler or question, a bad context , a model without a key."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "What each answer carries",
"url": "pages/live.html#observations",
"text": "Observation Is chunk_id , media_ts , frame_index Where the kept frame is. sampler_id , sampler , question Which answer this is, as in video_rag . frames , frame_ts Every frame the model was shown, in time order. description , structured The answer. content , vector What was embedded, and its vector. seen_at , answered_at , lag_s When the frame arrived and when its answer was ready (UTC), and the seconds between. gap_before The stream's clock jumped just before this frame. Each one is also appended to observations.jsonl as it arrives."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "Context frames",
"url": "pages/live.html#context",
"text": "One frame cannot show movement. context=(1, 0) sends the previous decimated frame too; (0, 1) the next one; (1, 1) both. A frame after the kept one delays its answer by one decimation interval (1 s at per_second=1 ); frames before cost nothing but tokens."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "When the model falls behind",
"url": "pages/live.html#falling-behind",
"text": "If frames are kept faster than the model answers, the oldest waiting frame is dropped and counted in run.dropped ; the lag stays bounded instead of growing. To keep up, raise the model's concurrency , keep fewer frames ( min_interval_s , max_per_chunk on the sampler), or lower per_second ."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "When the stream ends",
"url": "pages/live.html#results",
"text": "The run is written as media.json , timeline.json , manifest.json , descriptions.json and embedded.json , so search and aggregates read it like any other video. A chunk's description there is its frames' answers joined in time order, and each answer is kept whole under observations . LiveRun Is ended ended , stopped , stop_after_s or error . observations , failed , dropped Answers written, model calls that failed (the run goes on), frames dropped from the queue. written , unwritten Answers that reached database as they arrived, and those that did not. lag_s Seconds from arrival to answer: p50 , p95 , max . gaps Where the stream's clock jumped. duration_s , chunks , frames_decimated , frames_sampled How much was read. recording , steps , problems The recording's path, the documents written, and what failed. An exception from on_unit (other than StopStream ) stops the run, and is raised after the documents are written."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "Writing to a database as it runs",
"url": "pages/live.html#database",
"text": "from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Supabase from vidra.video_rag import search_observations, video_rag_live db = Supabase() run = video_rag_live(\"rtsp://dock-3.local/stream\", \"data/out\", video_id=\"dock-3\", sampler=\"clip:safety\", embedder=LocalEmbedder(), database=db) # from anywhere, while it runs: the last ten minutes on dock-3 hits = search_observations(\"liquid spilled on the floor\", \"dock-3\", since=datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(minutes=10), embedder=LocalEmbedder(), database=db) for h in hits: print(h.seen_at, h.media_ts, h.frame_index, h.description) With database= , every answer is sent as it arrives ( write_observations ): at once when the database keeps up, the backlog in one call when it does not. The video's row is written when the stream opens. A write that fails is counted in run.unwritten and the run goes on; every answer is still in observations.jsonl . When the stream ends, the batch documents follow, so search finds the run by chunk too. search_observations(query, video_id=None, embedder=None, limit=10, sampler=None, question=None, strategy=None, after=None, before=None, since=None, until=None, structured=None, video_ids=None, database=None, models=None) -> list[FrameHit] Ranks individual answers rather than chunks. A Folder reads each run's observations.jsonl in place, so it finds answers from a run still going. Argument Default Meaning query required The text to find; empty is refused. video_id , video_ids every run One id or a list. embedder , models OpenAI's The embedder the live run used. database \"supabase\" Where to search. limit 10 Answers to return. after , before none Stream seconds. since , until none When the frames arrived: a datetime or ISO 8601 (a naive one is UTC). sampler , question , strategy , structured none As in search . Each FrameHit has video_id , chunk_id , sampler_id , sampler , question , frame_index , media_ts , frames , description , structured , seen_at , score , dense_rank , text_rank ."
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "Logging important moments",
"url": "pages/live.html#moments",
"text": "To catch moments close to ones you describe (a worker without a hard hat, a spill, a blocked exit) as they happen, subclass your database and look at each answer in write_observations before it is stored. Nothing else is needed: the live run already calls it with every answer moments after it exists. It runs off the stream. The hook is called from the run's writer thread, so slow matching never delays answers. A bug in it does not stop the run. An exception is counted in run.unwritten ; catch your own errors, as below, so the answers are still stored. One run calls it one batch at a time. A database shared by several runs (several cameras) is called by each run's writer at once, so guard any state with a lock. Ask a question whose answers are easy to check, then check them two ways: Rules, exactly: one fixed-choice field per rule, with a way to say \"cannot tell\". row[\"structured\"][\"hard_hats\"] == \"a member of staff without one\" . Rules never go through similarity: embeddings handle negation badly, so \"a worker without a hard hat\" and \"a worker wearing a hard hat\" come out close. Without a \"cannot tell\" choice the model guesses: asked for a list of missing equipment, it reported missing safety glasses on 40 of 93 frames of a building site where nobody's eyes can be seen at that distance, and missing gloves on workers visibly wearing them. With one field per item and \"cannot tell\", it chose \"cannot tell\" 10 to 43 times per camera and the moments fell from 244 to 72. Ask only about what the camera can resolve (a hard hat, a vest), and say who counts: asked about \"workers\" in a shop, it counted the customers. Everything else, by similarity to each listed hazard, not to the whole answer. An answer is a paragraph about everything in shot, and one detail barely moves its vector: against whole answers, true ladder sightings scored at most 0.654 and a title card 0.653. Against each hazard on its own, true matches scored 0.83 to 0.91 (\"worker on step ladder\" 0.886, \"wet floor sign\" 0.911), and the closest false ones 0.75 to 0.81 (\"stacked pallets\" as a blocked exit, \"scattered materials on floor\" as a spill), hence 0.85 below. Measured with LocalEmbedder : a threshold belongs to an embedder and to footage, so measure your own. The model's judgement is the limit: checked against the frames, a \"without a hard hat\" flag on a building site was right (two of three workers in soft caps), and an \"everyone wears one\" on a warehouse frame was wrong (the driver in the cab was bare-headed). Treat a moment as worth a look, not as a verdict. docs/pages/examples/live_moments.py \"\"\"Log the moments a live stream shows that match ones you describe, as they arrive: a Supabase subclass that looks at each answer before storing it. python live_moments.py rtsp://camera/stream # or a file, read as a stream \"\"\" import json import sys import threading import numpy as np import vidra from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI, Supabase from vidra.video_rag import describe, video_rag_live vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") # A question whose answers are easy to check: one fixed-choice field per rule, # each with a way to say \"cannot tell\" (without one, the model guesses), and a # list of hazards, each a short phrase, for everything else. SEEN = [\"every member of staff wears one\", \"a member of staff without one\", \"cannot tell\", \"no staff visible\"] describe.add_question( \"ppe\", \"These {n} frames span {span}. Describe the staff at work (not customers or \" \"visitors) and any safety hazards.\", fields={ \"hard_hats\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"hard hats on the staff\", \"one_of\": SEEN}, \"hi_vis\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"high-visibility vests or clothing on \" \"the staff\", \"one_of\": SEEN}, \"hazards\": {\"type\": \"list\", \"about\": \"each hazard visible, in a few words\"}, }, ) RULES = {\"hard_hats\": \"no hard hat\", \"hi_vis\": \"no high-visibility clothing\"} # What to look for among the hazards, matched by similarity. TARGETS = {\"spill\": \"liquid spilled on the floor\", \"blocked_ex"
},
{
"page": "Live streams",
"title": "How it differs from video_rag",
"url": "pages/live.html#differences",
"text": "No audio. Speakers can only be told apart over the whole recording. Record the stream and run video_rag on the recording afterwards for the transcript. Uniform chunks only , and a short last chunk is not merged into the one before. Time starts at the first frame. A jump forward of more than 2 s is a gap; a jump backward (a reconnect) continues the clock instead of going back. Damaged packets are skipped and counted in the manifest, not fatal."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "Stages",
"url": "pages/stages.html",
"text": "The eight steps video_rag() runs, each callable on its own with all its settings. Each stage is a module under vidra.video_rag with three kinds of function: Function Takes Does the stage's own name: media.media , audio.audio , ... file paths reads its inputs, writes one output file, returns a receipt ( Produced ) a verb: split , listen , detect , timeline , ingest , apply , answer , encode documents already in memory the same work, returning the document; reads and writes no file load a path reads the stage's output back, typed The file function is the verb plus a read and a write, so both run the same checks. A receipt has .video_id , .component , .artifacts ( {name: path} ), .stats and .skipped . Full script: stage-by-stage recipe . Below, D is a video's folder. from pathlib import Path from vidra.video_rag import audio, boundaries, cut, describe, embed, media, video"
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "1. media",
"url": "pages/stages.html#media",
"text": "Reads the file's streams and makes the video's folder. Writes media.json . media.media(source, into, video_id=None, on_conflict=\"new\", name=None, recorded_at=None) -> Produced Argument Default Meaning source required The video file. into required The folder holding one folder per video. video_id filename stem The folder's name. on_conflict \"new\" When a different file holds the id: new , replace or refuse ( Video ids ). name , recorded_at from the file Display name and recording time (a datetime or ISO 8601 string). made = media.media(\"shop.mp4\", \"data/out\") D = Path(made.stats[\"folder\"]) # data/out/shop made.video_id # the id actually used media.split(path, video_id=None, name=None, recorded_at=None) returns the Media without writing; media.load(path) reads media.json . A file with no video or audio stream raises media.UnusableMedia ; on_conflict=\"refuse\" raises media.VideoIdTaken ."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "2. audio",
"url": "pages/stages.html#audio",
"text": "Transcribes and diarizes the whole soundtrack in one pass. Writes transcript.raw.json : words, segments and speaker turns with times, not yet chunked. Needs vidra[audio] . audio.audio(media, out, transcriber=\"whisper\", diarizer=\"pyannote\", model=None, language=None, vad_filter=None, compute_type=None, device=None, diarizer_model=None, exclusive=None) -> Produced Argument Default Meaning media required Path to media.json . out required Where to write transcript.raw.json . transcriber \"whisper\" whisper (faster-whisper), or stub (placeholder text, for tests). diarizer \"pyannote\" pyannote , or none : every segment keeps speaker: null . model \"small\" Whisper's model: tiny , base , small , medium , large-v3 , ... language detected Spoken language, e.g. \"en\" ; detected if not given. vad_filter True Skip stretches without speech. Off, Whisper can invent text over silence. compute_type float16 on a GPU, int8 on the CPU Whisper's precision. device cuda, else the CPU For both models. Whisper has no mps . diarizer_model \"pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1\" pyannote's pipeline. Gated: the first download needs HF_TOKEN from an account that accepted its terms. exclusive True Resolve overlapping speech so each word has one speaker. audio.audio(D / \"media.json\", D / \"transcript.raw.json\", model=\"medium\", language=\"en\", diarizer=\"pyannote\") A setting the chosen backends don't take is refused, e.g. language with transcriber=\"stub\" . A near-silent soundtrack is recorded as silent without running a model. audio.listen(media, ...) takes a Media and returns the RawTranscript . audio.load(path) reads one back."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "3–4. boundaries",
"url": "pages/stages.html#boundaries",
"text": "Two steps: evidence finds where content changes ( scene , vad , speaker only) and writes cuts.json ; boundaries turns it into chunks and writes timeline.json ."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "evidence",
"url": "pages/stages.html#evidence",
"text": "boundaries.evidence(out, policy, media=None, raw_transcript=None, stride=5, threshold=27.0, detect_width=320, silence_s=0.65) -> Produced Argument Default Policy Meaning out required Where to write cuts.json . policy required uniform (does nothing), scene , vad , speaker . media scene Path to media.json . raw_transcript vad, speaker Path to transcript.raw.json . stride 5 scene Score every Nth frame. Higher is faster but finds more false cuts. threshold 27.0 scene Change score needed for a cut (PySceneDetect's scale). Lower finds more. detect_width 320 scene Frames are scaled to this width before scoring. silence_s 0.65 vad A pause at least this long is a cut. A setting the policy doesn't read is refused ( boundaries.EVIDENCE_SETTINGS maps settings to policies). Scene scores are cached in cuts.json , so trying a new threshold needs no decode: boundaries.evidence(D / \"cuts.json\", \"scene\", media=D / \"media.json\", stride=5) for row in boundaries.calibrate(D / \"cuts.json\"): # nothing is decoded print(row[\"threshold\"], row[\"cuts\"], row[\"rate\"], row[\"median_gap_s\"]) boundaries.retune(D / \"cuts.json\", D / \"cuts.json\", threshold=35.0) # rewrite the cuts calibrate(cuts, thresholds=None) : how many cuts each threshold gives, as rows of threshold , cuts , rate (cuts per scored frame) and median_gap_s . cuts is a path or a Cuts ; thresholds defaults to a spread on the detector's scale. retune(cuts, out, threshold) : rewrites the cuts at a new threshold."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "boundaries",
"url": "pages/stages.html#grid",
"text": "boundaries.boundaries(media, out, policy=\"uniform\", cuts=None, chunk_s=20.0, min_s=5.0, max_s=None) -> Produced Argument Default Meaning media required Path to media.json . out required Where to write timeline.json . policy \"uniform\" As in evidence . cuts none Path to cuts.json ; required by every policy but uniform . chunk_s 20.0 The chunk length for uniform , and the default ceiling. min_s 5.0 Shorter chunks merge into a neighbour. max_s chunk_s Longer chunks split evenly (a 62 s span at 30 s becomes three of 20.8 s, not 30 + 30 + 2). boundaries.boundaries(D / \"media.json\", D / \"timeline.json\", policy=\"scene\", cuts=D / \"cuts.json\", min_s=10, max_s=40) grid = boundaries.load(D / \"timeline.json\") len(grid), grid.spans[0] # 12, (0.0, 19.93) A last chunk under a quarter of the chunk length joins the one before. min_s above the ceiling is refused. With no cuts, chunks are still capped at max_s . Verbs: detect(policy, media=None, transcript=None, stride=5, threshold=27.0, detect_width=320, silence_s=0.65) returns Cuts ( None for uniform ); timeline(media, policy=\"uniform\", cuts=None, chunk_s=20.0, min_s=5.0, max_s=None) returns the Timeline . m = media.split(\"shop.mp4\") grid = boundaries.timeline(m, \"scene\", cuts=boundaries.detect(\"scene\", media=m)) boundaries.POLICIES maps each policy to what its evidence reads: None , \"video\" or \"audio\" ."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "5. video",
"url": "pages/stages.html#video",
"text": "Decodes the picture once, offers frames to each sampler and stores the ones kept. Writes manifest.json and the JPEGs in store/ . See Samplers . video.video(media, timeline, out, store=None, sampler=\"uniform\", per_second=1.0, every_n=None, min_interval_s=0.0, max_per_chunk=None, threshold=None, vocabulary=None, confidence=None, languages=None, store_scope=\"sampled\", prune_store=False, on_progress=None) -> Produced Argument Default Meaning media , timeline required Paths to media.json and timeline.json . out required Where to write manifest.json . store none Frame folder. Without it no frames are kept and describe has nothing to read. sampler \"uniform\" A sampler spec : \"clip,yolo:overview\" , or a list of specs. per_second 1.0 Frames offered to the samplers per second of video. every_n 1 uniform : keep every Nth offered frame. min_interval_s 0.0 Every sampler: at least this many seconds between kept frames. max_per_chunk none Every sampler: at most this many frames per chunk. threshold per sampler clip , yolo , objects , text : keep a frame when similarity to the last kept one falls below this. vocabulary shop items objects : what to detect, e.g. [\"forklift\", \"pallet\"] . confidence 0.30 objects : how sure a detection must be. languages [\"en\"] text : EasyOCR's languages. store_scope \"sampled\" \"sampled\" stores kept frames; \"decimated\" stores every offered frame. prune_store False Delete frames this manifest doesn't use; otherwise the store keeps growing across runs. on_progress none Called with a Progress after each chunk. video.video(D / \"media.json\", D / \"timeline.json\", D / \"manifest.json\", store=D / \"store\", sampler=\"objects\", vocabulary=[\"cart\", \"basket\"], confidence=0.4, max_per_chunk=4) Samplers and questions are checked before decoding, and a setting no chosen sampler reads is refused (e.g. every_n without uniform ). No readable video stream raises video.UnreadableSource . video.ingest(media, timeline, sampler=\"uniform\", ..., frames=None, store_scope=\"sampled\", on_progress=None) takes a Media and Timeline , writes frames into frames (a FrameStore , or None ), and returns the Manifest . video.load(path) reads one back."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "The frame store",
"url": "pages/stages.html#frame-store",
"text": "video.FrameStore(root, quality=95, fmt=\"jpg\") writes one JPEG per kept frame into root , named by decode position; a frame kept twice is one file. quality is the JPEG quality. store = video.FrameStore(D / \"store\") plan = video.ingest(media.load(D / \"media.json\"), boundaries.load(D / \"timeline.json\"), \"clip\", frames=store)"
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "recreate",
"url": "pages/stages.html#recreate",
"text": "Rebuilds every frame from the manifest and the video, and can compare them byte for byte with an existing store: video.recreate(*, manifest, video, out, verify=None, force=False, quality=95) -> dict Argument Meaning manifest Path to manifest.json . video The video file it was built from. out Where to write the frames. verify An existing store to compare with. force Rebuild even if the video's size, rate or frame count differ from the manifest (otherwise video.Mismatch ); differences go in problems . quality JPEG quality the store was written at; must match for an identical rebuild. done = video.recreate(manifest=D / \"manifest.json\", video=\"shop.mp4\", out=\"rebuilt\", verify=D / \"store\") done[\"named\"], done[\"written\"], done[\"missing\"], done[\"problems\"] done[\"verified\"][\"identical\"] # True when every frame matches No file at video raises video.MissingVideo ."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "6. cut",
"url": "pages/stages.html#cut",
"text": "Cuts the raw transcript onto the grid; each word goes to the chunk its midpoint is in. Writes transcript.json . No model, so a new grid never re-runs Whisper. cut.cut(timeline, raw_transcript, out) -> Produced cut.cut(D / \"timeline.json\", D / \"transcript.raw.json\", D / \"transcript.json\") spoken = cut.load(D / \"transcript.json\") spoken.chunks[3][\"text\"], spoken.chunks[3][\"structured\"][\"speakers\"] cut.apply(timeline, raw) does it in memory. Silent chunks are kept with empty text, so chunk ids match every other file."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "7. describe",
"url": "pages/stages.html#describe",
"text": "Sends each chunk's frames to the vision model once per sampler and question. Writes descriptions.json . Calls run concurrently, up to the model's concurrency . describe.describe(manifest, timeline, store, out, previous=None, vlm=None, samplers=None, limit=None, max_output_tokens=None, on_progress=None) -> Produced Argument Default Meaning manifest , timeline required Paths to manifest.json and timeline.json . store required The frame folder video wrote. out required Where to write descriptions.json . previous none Earlier descriptions.json (usually out ); current answers are reused. vlm OpenAI() The vision model. samplers all Only these answer ids, e.g. [\"clip:text\"] ; others are kept from previous . limit none Max new calls this run; a later run with previous= continues. At least 1. max_output_tokens 2000 Cap on one answer; too low truncates structured answers. Changing it re-describes everything. on_progress none Called with a Progress after each call, in completion order. describe.describe(D / \"manifest.json\", D / \"timeline.json\", D / \"store\", D / \"descriptions.json\", previous=D / \"descriptions.json\", vlm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), limit=20) said = describe.load(D / \"descriptions.json\") answer = said.chunks[0][\"samplers\"][\"clip\"] answer[\"description\"] # the prose answer[\"structured\"] # the fields: {\"setting\": ..., \"people\": [...], ...} Frames are read only from the store: a missing store or frame raises describe.StoreUnavailable ; an unreachable model, describe.DescriberUnavailable . One failed call fails the run and its new answers are not written. describe.answer(manifest, timeline, frames, vlm=None, samplers=None, limit=None, existing=None, max_output_tokens=None, on_progress=None) works in memory; existing is an earlier Descriptions . Question functions are on Questions ."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "8. embed",
"url": "pages/stages.html#embed",
"text": "Turns every answer and every chunk's transcript into a unit of text and embeds it. Writes embedded.json : units and vectors under the embedder's key. embed.embed(out, descriptions=None, transcript=None, previous=None, timeline=None, embedder=None, batch=64, on_progress=None) -> Produced Argument Default Meaning out required Where to write embedded.json . descriptions , transcript none Paths to embed from; name at least one. previous none Earlier embedded.json (usually out ); unchanged units keep their vectors. timeline none Path to timeline.json , recorded as the units' grid. embedder OpenAIEmbedder() The embedder; search must use the same one. batch 64 Texts per embedding call. on_progress none Called with a Progress after each batch. embed.embed(D / \"embedded.json\", descriptions=D / \"descriptions.json\", transcript=D / \"transcript.json\", previous=D / \"embedded.json\", timeline=D / \"timeline.json\", embedder=LocalEmbedder()) index = embed.load(D / \"embedded.json\") index.embedder # \"local:BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5:384\" index.units[0][\"content\"], len(index.units[0][\"vector\"]) A unit's text is the answer's prose then its fields, keys sorted, so the same answer always gives the same vector. embed.encode(descriptions=None, transcript=None, previous=None, embedder=None, batch=64, on_progress=None) works in memory and returns a list of embed.Unit : video_id , chunk_id , sampler_id , sampler , question , content , structured , vector . An unreachable embedder raises embed.EmbedderUnavailable ."
},
{
"page": "Stages",
"title": "The whole chain in memory",
"url": "pages/stages.html#in-memory",
"text": "The verbs chain without an output folder; only frames are written, to the store you name: from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Stub m = media.split(\"shop.mp4\") raw = audio.listen(m) grid = boundaries.timeline(m, \"scene\", cuts=boundaries.detect(\"scene\", media=m)) store = video.FrameStore(\"frames/shop\") plan = video.ingest(m, grid, \"clip\", frames=store) spoken = cut.apply(grid, raw) said = describe.answer(plan, grid, store, vlm=Stub()) units = embed.encode(descriptions=said, transcript=spoken, embedder=LocalEmbedder())"
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "Samplers",
"url": "pages/samplers.html",
"text": "Which frames of each chunk are kept and sent to the vision model."
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "How sampling works",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#how",
"text": "The video is decoded once, however many samplers run. Frames are offered at per_second (default 1), by media time, so variable frame rates don't matter. Each sampler keeps the offered frames its strategy picks. The first frame of each chunk is always kept. min_interval_s and max_per_chunk apply before the strategy, so a frame they rule out costs no model time. Samplers reset at each chunk boundary: \"changed\" means changed within the chunk. Kept frames go to store/ (one file even if two samplers keep it) and are listed in manifest.json . Pass samplers to video_rag(sampler=...) , or to video.video along with their settings."
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "The samplers",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#list",
"text": "Sampler Keeps a frame when Model Install Its question answers uniform it is every every_n -th offered frame none core a scene description clip the whole picture has changed CLIP [local] a scene description yolo the people in view have changed YOLO + CLIP [local] one entry per person objects the objects you named have changed YOLO-World [local] one entry per object text the text on screen has changed EasyOCR's detector [local] each piece of text, transcribed"
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "uniform",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#uniform",
"text": "Keeps every every_n -th offered frame, counted from each chunk's start. No model. At per_second=1 , every_n=5 is one frame every 5 s; for a fixed interval in seconds use min_interval_s . For even coverage, or to ask something on a schedule: uniform:text reads the screen periodically with no OCR. Setting Default every_n 1 : every offered frame"
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "clip",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#clip",
"text": "Embeds each frame with CLIP ( openai/clip-vit-base-patch32 ) and keeps it when its similarity to the last kept frame drops below threshold , so slow pans still trigger once they drift far enough. The general-purpose choice. Setting Default Effect threshold 0.96 Lower keeps fewer frames."
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "yolo",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#yolo",
"text": "Finds people with YOLO ( yolo11n.pt ), embeds each person's crop with CLIP, and keeps the frame when someone in view no longer matches anyone in the last kept frame. People leaving don't trigger it. Crowds trigger often; pair with min_interval_s . Its question returns one entry per person: appearance , clothing , role , action and fixed-vocabulary attributes (gender, age group, hair, top and bottom colour and type, accessories). entities:people links these across chunks. Setting Default Effect threshold 0.83 Lower keeps fewer frames."
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "objects",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#objects",
"text": "Detects the objects in vocabulary with YOLO-World ( yolov8s-worldv2.pt ) and keeps the frame when detections no longer match the last kept frame's by class and position. Its question is told the vocabulary and returns one entry per object ( object , appearance , context ). Setting Default Effect vocabulary shopping bag, plastic bag, shopping cart, shopping basket, cardboard box, bottle, grocery item, cash register What to detect. Set it for your footage ; a mismatched list finds half as much and mislabels. confidence 0.30 Minimum detection confidence. threshold 0.30 Lower keeps fewer frames."
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "text",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#text",
"text": "Locates text with EasyOCR's detector (nothing is read here) and keeps the frame when the text layout changes. Its question transcribes each piece of text with its context. For slides, screens and signs. The most expensive sampler: the detector is ~98% of its time. If text changes on a schedule, uniform:text gets the same result without it. Setting Default Effect languages [\"en\"] EasyOCR language codes, e.g. [\"en\", \"de\"] . threshold 0.92 Lower keeps fewer frames."
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "Settings",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#settings",
"text": "Setting Read by Default per_second all (what is offered) 1.0 min_interval_s all 0.0 max_per_chunk all none every_n uniform 1 threshold clip , yolo , objects , text each sampler's own vocabulary objects shop items confidence objects 0.30 languages text [\"en\"] A setting no chosen sampler reads is refused. video.SAMPLER_SETTINGS is this table as data: {setting: (samplers)} . A value applies to every sampler that reads it: threshold=0.9 with clip,yolo sets both. from vidra.video_rag import video video.video(D / \"media.json\", D / \"timeline.json\", D / \"manifest.json\", store=D / \"store\", sampler=\"clip,objects\", threshold=0.9, vocabulary=[\"forklift\", \"pallet\", \"hard hat\"], confidence=0.4, min_interval_s=2.0, max_per_chunk=5)"
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "Choosing a threshold",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#thresholds",
"text": "Thresholds don't transfer between videos. clip at 0.96 on three similar shop videos: Video Frames kept Typical similarity, 1 s apart test.mp4 13.4% 0.9868 test2.mp4 18.0% 0.9895 test1.mp4 59.2% 0.9605 Busier footage keeps more. To control cost, use min_interval_s or max_per_chunk : they keep the most-changed frames and even out chunks. A lower threshold leaves busy chunks with many frames and quiet ones with one."
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "Sampler specs",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#specs",
"text": "The sampler argument names samplers and, optionally, their questions: Spec Means Answer ids clip clip's frames, clip's own question clip uniform:text every Nth frame, asked to read the screen uniform:text yolo:overview frames where people changed, as short prose yolo:overview clip:[text,scene] one pass, two questions clip:text , clip:scene clip:text+scene the same, without brackets clip:text , clip:scene clip,yolo two samplers, one decode clip , yolo clip,clip:checkout one clip pass, its own question and checkout clip , clip:checkout Specs naming the same sampler merge into one pass: clip:text,clip:scene is clip:[text,scene] . An extra question on the same frames costs one more call per chunk. Questions must exist (built in or added ); unknown ones are refused before decoding. Question names can't contain , : [ ] + . A list also works: sampler=[\"clip\", \"uniform:text\"] ."
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "Cost and hardware",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#cost",
"text": "RTX 4060 laptop, one frame per second: Samplers Video GPU CPU uniform any decode only: ~2 min for 3 hours of 720p clip , yolo , objects together 60 s 25 s 52 s text 60 s of slides 13 s 212 s Models run on CUDA, then mps , then CPU. Weights download on first use to weights/ (or VIDRA_WEIGHTS ); CLIP uses Hugging Face's cache."
},
{
"page": "Samplers",
"title": "Which to use",
"url": "pages/samplers.html#choosing",
"text": "Footage Try General, unknown content clip People matter (retail, security) clip,yolo , with min_interval_s for crowds Specific equipment or products objects with your vocabulary Slides, screen recordings text , or uniform:text to skip OCR Cheapest, or no GPU uniform with every_n 5 to 10 Short prose per chunk any sampler with :overview"
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "Questions",
"url": "pages/questions.html",
"text": "The prompt the vision model gets for each chunk: an instruction and the fields to fill."
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "What a question is",
"url": "pages/questions.html#what",
"text": "For each chunk, describe sends the kept frames with: An instruction , e.g. \"These 4 frames span 0:20–0:40 and were kept because the people in shot changed...\" A shape : the fields to fill, sent as a JSON Schema. Every answer also has a prose summary , the main text that gets embedded. Answers are stored under their answer id : description is the prose, structured the fields. Both are embedded; search can filter on fields. A bare sampler ( clip ) asks its own question; sampler:question ( clip:checkout ) asks another ( specs )."
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "Built-in questions",
"url": "pages/questions.html#builtin",
"text": "Question Asks Shape scene the segment as a whole: where, who and what, what happens, what changes scene uniform the same, for evenly spaced frames scene clip the same, then what changed from frame to frame scene yolo one entry per distinct person people objects one entry per distinct object, told what the detector looked for objects text each piece of text, transcribed exactly text overview what is happening, in 4 to 5 sentences; no fields prose"
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "Shapes",
"url": "pages/questions.html#shapes",
"text": "Shape Fields scene setting ; lists people (by appearance), objects , visible_text , actions , changes , tags . The fallback for questions without a shape. people people : one object per person with appearance , clothing , role , action , and fixed-vocabulary gender , age_group , hair_color , hair_style , top_color , top_type , bottom_color , bottom_type , accessories , distinguishing objects objects : one object per thing, with object , appearance , context text visible_text : one object per piece of text, with text , context prose none: a 4 to 5 sentence summary Every shape but prose asks for a summary of at least 150 words. Structured answers run ~3x longer than prose, hence max_output_tokens=2000 ."
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "Adding a question",
"url": "pages/questions.html#add",
"text": "describe.add_question(name, instruction, *, fields=None, shape=None, summary=None, about=\"\") -> dict from vidra.video_rag import describe describe.add_question( \"hazards\", \"These {n} frames span {span}. List every safety hazard you can see.\", fields={ \"hazards\": {\"type\": \"list\", \"about\": \"each hazard, briefly\"}, \"severity\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"the worst one\", \"one_of\": [\"none\", \"low\", \"high\"]}, \"exposed\": {\"type\": \"list\", \"about\": \"who is at risk\", \"of\": {\"who\": \"by appearance\", \"how\": \"how they are exposed\"}}, }, about=\"safety hazards and who is exposed\", ) video_rag(\"site.mp4\", \"data/out\", sampler=\"clip,clip:hazards\", models=models) Argument Meaning name Lowercase letters, digits, _ , - ; starts with a letter; up to 32 characters; not a built-in. instruction What the model is told. May use {n} (frame count), {span} (the chunk's time span) and {vocabulary} (the objects vocabulary). fields The answer's own fields ( below ). shape Instead of fields , a built-in shape: scene , people , objects , text or prose . summary With fields : prose length, \"standard\" (150+ words, default) or \"brief\" (4 to 5 sentences). about One-line description. With neither fields nor shape , the answer is prose only. Re-adding a custom name replaces it. Returns question(name) ."
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "The fields",
"url": "pages/questions.html#fields",
"text": "Each field is a dict: Key Meaning type \"text\" (a string) or \"list\" . about Required. What goes in the field. one_of Allowed values. Use it for anything you'll filter on; free text varies ( cashier , cashier or customer ). of For a list: make each entry an object, {key: what goes there} , keeping who-did-what together. Field names: lowercase letters, digits, _ , starting with a letter. Limits: 12 fields, 8 keys per of , 24 values per one_of . Invalid questions are refused when added, not mid-run."
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "Listing and removing",
"url": "pages/questions.html#manage",
"text": "describe.questions() # every question name, built in or added describe.question(\"hazards\") # {\"name\", \"instruction\", \"about\", \"builtin\", # \"shape\", \"summary\", \"fields\": {field: about}} describe.remove_question(\"hazards\") # answers already stored are kept Saved in prompts.json under the data root. Hand edits work; a malformed entry is dropped with a warning. A built-in's name raises describe.ProtectedPrompt ; other problems raise describe.PromptError , listing each. A run naming a removed question is refused."
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "Searching by a question",
"url": "pages/questions.html#search",
"text": "from vidra.video_rag import search moments, notes = search(\"someone near the edge\", \"site\", question=\"hazards\", structured={\"severity\": \"high\"}, models=models, database=db) moments[0].hits[0][\"structured\"] # {\"hazards\": [...], \"severity\": \"high\", \"exposed\": [...]} question= keeps that question's answers from any sampler. structured= keeps answers whose field equals the value, or whose list contains it ( Search )."
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "Editing a question",
"url": "pages/questions.html#reuse",
"text": "Each question's wording is hashed with its answers. Editing a question re-describes only its answers; adding one changes nothing stored. Changing the vision model or max_output_tokens re-describes everything."
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "Questions and aggregate prompts",
"url": "pages/questions.html#vs-prompts",
"text": "Both are an instruction plus fields: describe.add_question aggregates.add_prompt Answered by the VLM the LLM Reads one chunk's frames text video_rag already extracted: transcript, answers Answers once per chunk once per video, or per chapter or item Run by a sampler spec: clip:hazards aggregates.custom(name=...) , or aggregate(hazard_report=...) Saved in prompts.json aggregates.json See Custom prompts and profiles ."
},
{
"page": "Questions",
"title": "Complete example",
"url": "pages/questions.html#example",
"text": "docs/pages/examples/custom_question.py \"\"\"A question of your own: what the vision model is asked about each chunk, and the fields its answer must fill. Then search by those fields. python custom_question.py path/to/video.mp4 \"\"\" import sys import vidra from vidra import Folder, LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI from vidra.video_rag import describe, search, video_rag vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") source = sys.argv[1] models = Models(vlm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), embedder=LocalEmbedder()) database = Folder(\"data/out\") # Saved in data/prompts.json; adding it again replaces it. describe.add_question( \"checkout\", \"These {n} frames span {span}. Describe what happens at the checkout.\", fields={ \"payment\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"how the customer pays, if it can be seen\", \"one_of\": [\"cash\", \"card\", \"phone\", \"none visible\"]}, \"items\": {\"type\": \"list\", \"about\": \"each item scanned, bagged or handed over\"}, \"people\": {\"type\": \"list\", \"about\": \"each person at the checkout\", \"of\": {\"role\": \"cashier, customer or bystander\", \"doing\": \"what their hands are doing\"}}, }, about=\"the checkout: payment, items, who does what\", ) print(describe.question(\"checkout\")[\"fields\"]) # clip's frames, asked clip's own question and ours, in one decode. run = video_rag(source, \"data/out\", policy=\"scene\", sampler=\"clip,clip:checkout\", models=models, database=database) # Only answers to our question, and only those that saw cash. moments, notes = search(\"a customer paying\", run.video_id, question=\"checkout\", structured={\"payment\": \"cash\"}, models=models, database=database) for m in moments: answer = m.hits[0][\"structured\"] print(f\"{m.start_ts:6.1f}-{m.end_ts:6.1f}s payment={answer['payment']} \" f\"items={answer['items'][:3]}\") for note in notes: print(\"note:\", note)"
},
{
"page": "Search",
"title": "Search",
"url": "pages/search.html",
"text": "Find the chunks that match a text query."
},
{
"page": "Search",
"title": "Searching",
"url": "pages/search.html#basics",
"text": "from vidra import Folder, LocalEmbedder, Models from vidra.video_rag import search models = Models(embedder=LocalEmbedder()) # the embedder that built the index db = Folder(\"data/out\") # or Supabase() moments, notes = search(\"a customer paying in cash\", \"shop\", models=models, database=db) for m in moments: print(m.video_id, m.chunk_id, m.start_ts, m.end_ts, round(m.score, 4)) for hit in m.hits: # the answers that matched in this chunk print(\" \", hit[\"sampler_id\"], hit[\"content\"][:80]) Search reads a database: the one the run exported to, or a Folder over the output. Use the embedder that built the index; other embedders' units are invisible."
},
{
"page": "Search",
"title": "Arguments",
"url": "pages/search.html#arguments",
"text": "search(query, video_id=None, embedder=None, moments=5, sampler=None, candidates=20, question=None, strategy=None, chunk_ids=None, window=0, after=None, before=None, structured=None, video_ids=None, grids=None, database=None, models=None) -> (list[Moment], list[str]) Argument Default Meaning query required The text to find; empty is refused. video_id every video One id, or a list of ids. video_ids none A list of ids; same as a list in video_id . embedder OpenAIEmbedder() The embedder. Or put it in models . models none A Models ; only embedder is used. database \"supabase\" Where to search: a Database , or a name. moments 5 How many chunks to return. candidates 20 Units ranked before grouping into chunks. Raise it if filters or many samplers leave too few moments. question none Only this question's answers, from any sampler: \"text\" matches clip:text and uniform:text . sampler none Only this answer id: \"clip:text\" , \"yolo\" , \"transcript\" . strategy none Only this sampler's answers, any question: \"clip\" . structured none Exact field values: {\"payment\": \"cash\"} . A list field matches if it contains the value. chunk_ids none Only these chunks. after , before none Only chunks overlapping this window, in seconds. window 0 With chunk_ids or after / before : widen by this many chunks each side. grids none {video_id: timeline.json path} : read chunk times from the file, not the database. # only what was read off the screen, between minute 2 and minute 5 search(\"the error message\", \"talk\", question=\"text\", after=120, before=300, models=models, database=db) # only clip's answers to the checkout question, where a card was used search(\"paying\", \"shop\", sampler=\"clip:checkout\", structured={\"payment\": \"card\"}, models=models, database=db) # across two videos search(\"a forklift reversing\", [\"monday\", \"tuesday\"], moments=10, models=models, database=db)"
},
{
"page": "Search",
"title": "What comes back",
"url": "pages/search.html#results",
"text": "A list of Moment , best first, and a list of notes. Moment Is video_id Which video. chunk_id Which chunk of that video. start_ts , end_ts The chunk's start and end, in seconds. score A rank score for ordering, not a similarity ( below ). hits The matching answers in this chunk, best first. samplers The answer ids of the hits. as_dict() The moment as plain data. Each hit has sampler_id (the answer id), sampler , question , content (the embedded text), structured (the fields), dense_rank (vector rank) and text_rank (full-text rank, or None ). Read the notes when results look wrong or empty; they explain why. If nothing is indexed for this embedder at all, search raises MissingArtifact (a FileNotFoundError )."
},
{
"page": "Search",
"title": "How ranking works",
"url": "pages/search.html#ranking",
"text": "The query is embedded with the embedder's embed_query . The database ranks candidates units under that embedder, after filters. Supabase fuses vector similarity and Postgres full-text search by reciprocal rank: full text catches exact words and names, vectors catch paraphrases. Folder uses vectors only. Units are grouped by chunk. A chunk scores 1/(10 + best) + 0.5/(10 + second) , so more answers alone don't win. Filters leave fewer units per chunk, so scores drop; the notes say so."
},
{
"page": "Search",
"title": "Getting better results",
"url": "pages/search.html#tips",
"text": "Describe the moment: \"a man hands the cashier a banknote\" beats \"cash payment\". Several samplers give each chunk several accounts; agreement lifts the right chunk. For exact filtering, add a question with a one_of field and use structured= ( fields ). Use Supabase for names, numbers and exact phrases; Folder has no full-text search."
},
{
"page": "Search",
"title": "Searching summaries, chapters and people",
"url": "pages/search.html#aggregates",
"text": "To find a video by its summary, a chapter, or a linked person or object, use aggregates.search ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Aggregates",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html",
"text": "Whole-video answers: counts, speakers, summaries, chapters, events, recurring people and objects."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "From files to an answer",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#flow",
"text": "files ──► record ──► input ──► aggregator ──► answer file (what exists) (what to read) (what to ask) A record is a video's documents, by path. An input is what one aggregator reads, built from the record. Nothing is read by default: you name the transcript, answers and fields. An aggregator reads one input and writes one answer file. from pathlib import Path from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI, aggregates models = Models(llm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), embedder=LocalEmbedder()) D = Path(\"data/out/shop\") # a folder video_rag wrote video = aggregates.record(timeline=D / \"timeline.json\", transcript=D / \"transcript.json\", descriptions=D / \"descriptions.json\") told = video.excerpt(transcript=True, answers={\"clip\": [\"summary\"]}) aggregates.summary(input=told, out=D / \"answers\" / \"summary.json\", models=models) print(aggregates.load(D / \"answers\" / \"summary.json\").payload[\"summary\"]) Aggregates never open the video or need a database. Full script: aggregates recipe ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Records",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#record",
"text": "aggregates.record(*, timeline, transcript=None, descriptions=None, manifest=None) -> Record Argument Meaning timeline Required: timeline.json . transcript transcript.json , for anything that reads speech. descriptions descriptions.json , for anything that reads the answers. manifest manifest.json ; only stats reads it (frames counted). Documents from another video or grid are refused ( aggregates.RecordError ). A Record has .video_id , .timeline and three methods: video.answer_ids() # [\"clip\", \"clip:checkout\", \"yolo\"]: the answers it holds"
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "excerpt: text per chunk",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#excerpt",
"text": "Record.excerpt(*, transcript=False, answers=None, out=None) -> Excerpt Text per chunk, for text aggregators: the transcript (if transcript=True ) and the listed fields of each named answer. \"summary\" is the prose; other names are fields. said = video.excerpt(transcript=True) seen = video.excerpt(answers={\"clip\": [\"summary\"], \"clip:checkout\": [\"summary\", \"payment\", \"items\"]}) both = video.excerpt(transcript=True, answers={\"clip\": [\"summary\", \"actions\"]}) Answer ids match exactly. An unknown answer or field is refused here, listing what exists. Chunks with nothing selected are left out."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "sightings: entries to link",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#sightings",
"text": "Record.sightings(*, profile, answers=None, keys=None, out=None) -> Sightings For linking profiles: every entry of the profile's list field in the named answers. For people , each person in each yolo answer is one sighting. people = video.sightings(profile=\"people\", answers=[\"yolo\"]) by_clothes = video.sightings(profile=\"people\", answers=[\"yolo\"], keys=[\"clothing\"]) keys narrows the profile's identity keys; it can't add new ones."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Saving inputs",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#saved-inputs",
"text": "out= also writes the input to a file. Aggregators accept that path in place of the object; aggregates.load_input(path) reads it back. video.excerpt(transcript=True, out=D / \"inputs\" / \"said.json\") aggregates.summary(input=D / \"inputs\" / \"said.json\", out=D / \"summary.json\", models=models)"
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "The aggregators",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#aggregators",
"text": "Tiers: free ones count, local ones run a small local model ( vidra[local] ), llm ones call the LLM. Aggregator Tier Reads Answers stats free record duration, chunk lengths, words, words per minute, frames and answers counted coverage free record how many chunks have picture, sound, both or neither speakers free record with a transcript speakers, turns, handovers, speech ratio, the dominant speaker ner local excerpt named entities (GLiNER) and the chunks each appears in sentiment local excerpt tone per chunk (DistilBERT), overall, and where it turns summary llm excerpt a summary, topics, setting, notable moments chapters llm excerpt consecutive chapters with titles, summaries and times events llm excerpt discrete events, each tied to a chunk entities llm sightings the same person, object or text linked across chunks, with an account of each custom llm excerpt a prompt of your own ( Custom prompts ) Each writes one answer to out and returns a receipt ( .artifacts , .stats ). All take previous= , an earlier answer reused if still current. LLM ones take models= , or llm= and embedder= . Nothing to answer raises aggregates.Inapplicable with the reason."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "stats, coverage, speakers",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#stats",
"text": "aggregates.stats(*, record, out, previous=None) aggregates.coverage(*, record, out, previous=None) aggregates.speakers(*, record, out, previous=None) aggregates.stats(record=video, out=D / \"answers\" / \"stats.json\") Answer Payload stats duration_s , chunks , chunk_s ( min , median , max ), policy , derived_from , frames_sampled , descriptions_by_sampler , words , chunks_with_speech , words_per_minute coverage both , picture_only , sound_only , neither (chunk counts), silent_chunks , chunks (each with chunk_id , start_ts , end_ts , sources ) speakers speakers (count), turns , handovers , monologue , speech_s , speech_ratio , by_speaker (each speaker , seconds , share ), dominant"
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "ner",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#ner",
"text": "aggregates.ner(*, input, out, previous=None, labels=None, threshold=None, model=None) Setting Default Meaning labels person, organisation, location, product, event, date What kinds of name to find. GLiNER takes any label: [\"drug\", \"dosage\"] works. threshold 0.5 How sure the model must be. model urchade/gliner_small-v2.1 A GLiNER model on Hugging Face. Payload: entities (each text , label , chunk_ids , mentions ), count , by_label , chunks_read , labels , model ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "sentiment",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#sentiment",
"text": "aggregates.sentiment(*, input, out, previous=None, model=None) model defaults to distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english . Payload: per_chunk (each chunk_id , start_ts , end_ts , label , score , signed from -1 to 1), mean , positive_chunks , negative_chunks , turning_points , chunks_read , model ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "summary",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#summary",
"text": "aggregates.summary(*, input, out, previous=None, models=None, llm=None) Summarises rows in groups, then the group summaries, until one is left, so any length fits. Payload: summary (at least 150 words, citing chunk ids like [3] ), topics , setting , notable , chunks_read , reduction_levels , layers (each intermediate summary), word_count ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "chapters",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#chapters",
"text": "aggregates.chapters(*, input, out, previous=None, models=None, llm=None, embedder=None, max_spans=None, min_span_s=None) The embedder places boundaries where neighbouring chunks are least alike; the LLM names each chapter. Times come from the grid. Setting Default Meaning max_spans none At most this many chapters: the two most alike neighbours merge until it fits. min_span_s 30 The shortest chapter, in seconds; shorter ones merge into the more alike neighbour. 0 turns it off. Payload: chapters (each title , summary , chunk_ids , start_ts , end_ts ), count , covers_all_chunks , uncovered , segmentation (boundaries, their similarity and depth, and merges)."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "events",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#events",
"text": "aggregates.events(*, input, out, previous=None, models=None, llm=None) Reads 100 chunks at a time. Each event cites a chunk; times come from the grid. Payload: events (each what , kind of action , arrival , change or speech , chunk_id , start_ts , end_ts ), count , windows ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "entities",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#entities",
"text": "aggregates.entities(*, profile, input, out, previous=None, models=None, llm=None, embedder=None) people = video.sightings(profile=\"people\", answers=[\"yolo\"]) aggregates.entities(profile=\"people\", input=people, out=D / \"answers\" / \"people.json\", models=models) Linking uses embeddings and rules, not the model: identity fields are embedded, and since two entries in one answer are different people, their similarity sets this video's linking threshold. The LLM writes an account per entity and flags contradicting observations as doubts rather than dropping them. Built-in profile Links entries of Identity From the answers of people people appearance , clothing , plus the fixed attributes yolo , or any question with the people shape objects objects object , appearance objects text visible_text text text Payload: entities , each with entity_id , label , appearances , chunk_ids , start_ts , end_ts , observed_s , mentions (each sighting), account (the profile's fields, e.g. description , narrative , role ) and doubts ; also count , linked , narrated , together (pairs seen in the same chunks), and linking (the threshold and how it was set). Stored as entities.people.json . Your own profiles: add_profile ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "custom",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#custom",
"text": "aggregates.custom(*, name, input, out, previous=None, models=None, llm=None, embedder=None, **settings) Runs a prompt aggregator by name: one from add_prompt , or a built-in ( custom(name=\"summary\") equals summary() ). spans prompts also take embedder , max_spans , min_span_s . Custom prompts ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Several at once: aggregate()",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#aggregate",
"text": "aggregates.aggregate(*, out, models=None, database=None, previous=None, settings=None, llm=None, embedder=None, **aggregators) -> Produced Runs the aggregators given, cheapest first. Each keyword is an aggregator; its value is the input. done = aggregates.aggregate( out=D / \"aggregates\", previous=D / \"aggregates\", # reuse answers that are still current models=models, database=db, # optional copy (see Databases) stats=video, speakers=video, ner=said, summary=both, chapters=both, events=seen, entities_people=people, # entities:people incident_report=seen, # a custom prompt, by its name sentiment={\"spoken\": said, \"seen\": seen}, # two answers: sentiment~spoken, ~seen settings={\"ner\": {\"labels\": [\"person\"]}, \"chapters\": {\"max_spans\": 4}}, ) done.artifacts # {\"summary\": \".../summary.json\", \"sentiment~spoken\": ..., ...} done.stats[\"computed\"] # how many were run rather than reused done.stats[\"skipped\"] # {\"speakers\": \"needs a transcript ...\"} done.stats[\"problems\"] # database writes that failed Argument Meaning out The folder for the answers. What each one read is saved in out/inputs/ . previous A folder of earlier answers (usually out ). models , llm , embedder Who answers. database Also export the answers, and embed the summary, chapters and entity accounts for aggregates.search . settings {aggregator: {setting: value}} . **aggregators Each aggregator by name ( entities:people as entities_people ), with its input: a Record , an excerpt, sightings, a saved input's path, or a dict of labelled inputs for several answers from one aggregator. aggregates.validate(settings=None, llm=None, embedder=None, **aggregators) takes the same keywords and lists every problem without running."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Reading answers",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#reading",
"text": "answer = aggregates.load(D / \"aggregates\" / \"summary.json\") answer.aggregate_id # \"summary\" answer.tier # \"llm\" answer.payload[\"summary\"] answer.stats[\"model\"] # \"openai:gpt-5.4-mini\": who wrote it answer.inputs_fingerprint # a hash of the text it read aggregates.answers(D / \"aggregates\") # [\"chapters\", \"entities:people\", \"stats\", ...] aggregates.load_all(D / \"aggregates\") # {id: answer}; an absent folder is {} load(path) reads one answer; answers(directory) lists a folder's ids; load_all(directory) reads them all. aggregates.answer(name, data, answer_id=None, llm=None, embedder=None, previous=None, settings=None, models=None) runs one aggregator in memory, writing nothing. previous is an answer to reuse; answer_id names it ( \"sentiment~spoken\" )."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Reuse",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#reuse",
"text": "An answer is reused when its input text, definition version and model key all match. Changing any of them, or a setting like max_spans , recomputes it. Reused answers are still written to out ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Several videos as one",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#combine",
"text": "aggregates.combine(*, records, out, video_id=None) -> Record monday = aggregates.record(timeline=\"data/out/monday/timeline.json\", transcript=\"data/out/monday/transcript.json\") tuesday = aggregates.record(timeline=\"data/out/tuesday/timeline.json\", transcript=\"data/out/tuesday/transcript.json\") week = aggregates.combine(records=[monday, tuesday], out=\"data/out/week\") aggregates.summary(input=week.excerpt(transcript=True), out=\"data/out/week/summary.json\", models=models) Videos are laid end to end on one clock: chunks renumbered, times shifted, speakers prefixed with their video. The result is written to out and returned as a record any aggregator reads. Naming a video twice is refused. aggregates.merge(parts, video_id=None) does it in memory; each part is a combination.Part(timeline, descriptions=None, transcript=None, manifest=None) . Linking over a combination links across videos too, lookalikes included."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Searching aggregates",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#search",
"text": "aggregates.search(query, level=\"source\", embedder=None, limit=5, source_ids=None, database=None, models=None) -> list[dict] With a database, aggregate() also embeds three kinds of text, each searched at its own level: level Finds By \"source\" which video its summary \"span\" which part, with a time span each chapter \"entity\" who or what each linked entity's account videos = aggregates.search(\"a busy checkout\", level=\"source\", models=models, database=db) parts = aggregates.search(\"customers paying\", level=\"span\", limit=10, models=models, database=db) who = aggregates.search(\"a man in a red cap\", level=\"entity\", models=models, database=db) parts[0][\"source_id\"], parts[0][\"aggregate_id\"], parts[0][\"item_id\"] parts[0][\"start_ts\"], parts[0][\"end_ts\"], parts[0][\"content\"] Returns the best limit units of that level for query , each with source_id , video_ids , aggregate_id , item_id , level , content , start_ts , end_ts and ranks. Levels are never mixed. source_ids limits the sources. Use the embedder the aggregates were exported with."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Looking up aggregators",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#introspection",
"text": "aggregates.available() # every aggregator id, built in and added aggregates.about(\"chapters\") # \"a table of contents: contiguous chapters ...\" aggregates.tier_of(\"ner\") # \"local\" aggregates.kind_of(\"summary\") # \"fold\"; None for one written as code; \"link\" for a profile aggregates.settings_of(\"ner\") # [\"model\", \"labels\", \"threshold\"] aggregates.uses_embedder(\"chapters\") # True aggregates.takes_inputs(\"stats\") # False: it reads a record Lower level: aggregates.build(name, llm=None, embedder=None, **settings) constructs an aggregator; aggregates.missing(aggregator, context) says why one can't run on a Context ; aggregates.definition_rows(used) gives the definition rows a database stores. aggregates.REGISTRY holds the free aggregators, aggregates.RUNNERS the class per prompt kind, aggregates.TIERS is (\"free\", \"local\", \"llm\") ."
},
{
"page": "Aggregates",
"title": "Errors",
"url": "pages/aggregates.html#errors",
"text": "Class Raised when aggregates.RecordError a record cannot be opened, or an input asks for an answer, field or profile the record lacks aggregates.AggregateError an aggregator is handed the wrong kind of input, or does not exist aggregates.Inapplicable there is nothing to answer; aggregate() reports it as skipped aggregates.DefinitionError a prompt or profile is invalid or unknown aggregates.ProtectedDefinition you tried to change a built-in"
},
{
"page": "Custom prompts and profiles",
"title": "Custom prompts and profiles",
"url": "pages/definitions.html",
"text": "Your own aggregators: a prompt asks the LLM about the whole video; a linking profile follows one kind of thing across chunks. The built-in summary , chapters , events are prompts and entities:people , entities:objects , entities:text are profiles. Yours are saved in aggregates.json under the data root and run the same way."
},
{
"page": "Custom prompts and profiles",
"title": "Prompts",
"url": "pages/definitions.html#prompts",
"text": "aggregates.add_prompt(name, instruction, fields, *, kind=\"fold\", key=None, fold_instruction=None, about=\"\") -> dict from vidra import aggregates aggregates.add_prompt( \"incident_report\", \"Write an incident report for this video.\", fields={ \"report\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"what happened, in order\"}, \"severity\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"how serious it was\", \"one_of\": [\"none\", \"minor\", \"major\"]}, }, kind=\"fold\", ) aggregates.custom(name=\"incident_report\", input=seen, out=\"data/out/shop/answers/incident_report.json\", models=models) Argument Meaning name Lowercase letters, digits, _ , - , starting with a letter. Not a built-in, stats , speakers , coverage , ner , sentiment or entities . instruction What the LLM is told; the chunks' text follows, tagged with chunk ids. fields The answer's fields, as for questions: type , about , one_of , of ( fields ). kind fold , spans or items ( below ). key For spans and items : the answer's list name (default: the kind). fold_instruction For fold : the instruction for summarising each intermediate group. about One-line description. Returns the stored definition. Re-adding a name replaces it."
},
{
"page": "Custom prompts and profiles",
"title": "The three kinds",
"url": "pages/definitions.html#kinds",
"text": "Kind Answers How Like fold one answer for the whole video Rows are summarised in groups, then the summaries, until one is left. Any length. summary spans a list of consecutive parts, each filling fields , with chunk_ids , start_ts , end_ts The embedder places boundaries; the LLM fills each part's fields. Takes max_spans , min_span_s and an embedder. chapters items a list of things, each filling fields , with chunk_id , start_ts , end_ts Read 100 chunks at a time; each item cites its chunk, and times come from the grid. events aggregates.add_prompt( \"handovers\", \"List every moment something is handed from one person to another.\", fields={\"what\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"what was handed over\"}, \"between\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"who gave it to whom\"}}, kind=\"items\", key=\"handovers\") aggregates.add_prompt( \"acts\", \"Divide this performance into acts.\", fields={\"title\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"a short title\"}, \"mood\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"the mood\", \"one_of\": [\"calm\", \"tense\", \"comic\"]}}, kind=\"spans\", key=\"acts\") aggregates.custom(name=\"acts\", input=both, out=D / \"answers\" / \"acts.json\", models=models, max_spans=4)"
},
{
"page": "Custom prompts and profiles",
"title": "Running a prompt",
"url": "pages/definitions.html#running",
"text": "aggregates.custom(name=..., input=..., out=..., models=...) ( custom ). As a keyword of aggregates.aggregate : aggregate(out=..., incident_report=seen) . workflow at tier=\"llm\" runs every added prompt. Editing a prompt recomputes its answers on the next run."
},
{
"page": "Custom prompts and profiles",
"title": "Linking profiles",
"url": "pages/definitions.html#profiles",
"text": "Links the entries of one list field across chunks (each person in people ) into entities, then the LLM writes an account of each. Linking uses embeddings and rules, not the LLM. aggregates.add_profile(name, field, instruction, fields, *, identity=None, story=None, transcript=None, threshold=None, rule=None, mutual=None, check=None, min_appearances=None, max_narratives=None, weights=None, attributes=None, near=None, shared=None, about=\"\") -> dict aggregates.add_profile( \"tools\", \"objects\", \"These may be the same object, seen in different chunks. Say what it is and who used it.\", fields={\"use\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"who used it, and for what\"}}, identity=[\"object\", \"appearance\"], story=[\"context\"], ) tools = video.sightings(profile=\"tools\", answers=[\"objects\"]) aggregates.entities(profile=\"tools\", input=tools, out=D / \"answers\" / \"tools.json\", models=models) # answer id: entities:tools Argument Default Meaning name required Runs as entities:<name> . field required The list field to link, e.g. people , objects , or one of your question's. instruction required The account instruction; numbered observations follow in time order. fields required The account's fields. identity [] Keys that identify an entry ( [\"appearance\", \"clothing\"] ). Without them the whole entry is compared and threshold is required. story [] Extra keys the account reads ( [\"role\", \"action\"] ). transcript False Also give the account the transcript of the entity's chunks. threshold read off the video Fixed cosine similarity (0 to 1) to link above. Required without identity ; refused with weights or attributes . rule \"max\" How the threshold is set from pairs known to differ (two entries in one answer): \"max\" above the most similar pair; \"q95\" above the 95th percentile (links more). mutual True Link only mutual best matches. check \"flag\" \"flag\" : the LLM marks contradicting observations as doubts . \"off\" : no check. min_appearances 2 Minimum sightings for an account. max_narratives 12 Maximum accounts (up to 50). weights none {identity key: weight} : embed each key separately and weight them. attributes none {key: weight} for fixed-vocabulary keys ( gender , top_color ) whose agreement also counts. near none Attribute values that count as nearly equal: [[\"dark_blue\", \"black\"], [\"jacket\", \"coat\"]] . shared none {key: weight} : credit for shared accessories or distinguishing words. about \"\" One-line description. The built-in people profile uses weights , attributes , near , shared and rule=\"q95\" ; objects and text use one embedding and rule=\"max\" . aggregates.definition(\"entities:people\") shows one in full. In aggregate(...) , write the colon as an underscore: entities_tools=tools ."
},
{
"page": "Custom prompts and profiles",
"title": "Listing and removing",
"url": "pages/definitions.html#manage",
"text": "aggregates.definition(\"incident_report\") # the stored entry, with \"name\", \"kind\", \"builtin\" aggregates.definition(\"entities:people\") # a profile; its kind is \"link\" aggregates.available() # every aggregator id, yours included aggregates.remove_prompt(\"incident_report\") # answers already written are kept aggregates.remove_profile(\"tools\") Changing a built-in raises aggregates.ProtectedDefinition . Invalid definitions raise aggregates.DefinitionError when added; .problems lists each issue."
},
{
"page": "Custom prompts and profiles",
"title": "Complete example",
"url": "pages/definitions.html#example",
"text": "docs/pages/examples/custom_aggregate.py \"\"\"Aggregators of your own: a prompt run over the whole video, and a linking profile that follows one kind of thing across chunks. python custom_aggregate.py data/out/<video_id> \"\"\" import sys from pathlib import Path import vidra from vidra import LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI, aggregates vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") D = Path(sys.argv[1]) models = Models(llm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), embedder=LocalEmbedder()) video = aggregates.record(timeline=D / \"timeline.json\", transcript=D / \"transcript.json\", descriptions=D / \"descriptions.json\") told = video.excerpt(transcript=True, answers={\"clip\": [\"summary\"]}) # fold: one answer over the whole video. aggregates.add_prompt( \"incident_report\", \"Write an incident report for this video.\", fields={ \"report\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"what happened, in order\"}, \"severity\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"how serious it was\", \"one_of\": [\"none\", \"minor\", \"major\"]}, \"people_involved\": {\"type\": \"list\", \"about\": \"each person involved, by appearance\"}, }, kind=\"fold\", about=\"an incident report with a severity\", ) # items: discrete things, each citing the chunk it is in. aggregates.add_prompt( \"handovers\", \"List every moment something is handed from one person to another.\", fields={ \"what\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"what was handed over\"}, \"between\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"who gave it to whom, by appearance\"}, }, kind=\"items\", key=\"handovers\", ) aggregates.custom(name=\"incident_report\", input=told, out=D / \"answers\" / \"incident_report.json\", models=models) report = aggregates.load(D / \"answers\" / \"incident_report.json\").payload print(report[\"severity\"], \"-\", report[\"report\"][:200]) # Linking: the same object across chunks, from the `objects` field of the # `objects` sampler's answers (video_rag with sampler=\"objects\"). aggregates.add_profile( \"tools\", \"objects\", \"These may be the same object, seen in different chunks. Say what it is \" \"and who used it for what.\", fields={\"use\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"about\": \"who used it, and for what\"}}, identity=[\"object\", \"appearance\"], # what decides that two entries are one story=[\"context\"], # what the account reads besides ) # All of them run in the pipeline too, each a keyword named after it # (`entities:tools` is spelled `entities_tools`). inputs = {\"incident_report\": told, \"handovers\": told} if \"objects\" in video.answer_ids(): inputs[\"entities_tools\"] = video.sightings(profile=\"tools\", answers=[\"objects\"]) done = aggregates.aggregate(out=D / \"aggregates\", previous=D / \"aggregates\", models=models, **inputs) print(\"wrote:\", sorted(done.artifacts)) print(aggregates.definition(\"handovers\"))"
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Models",
"url": "pages/models.html",
"text": "The three model roles, the ready-made classes, and writing your own."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Roles",
"url": "pages/models.html#roles",
"text": "Role Base class Used by Default vlm VLM describe : frames in, an answer out OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\") llm LLM the llm aggregators: summary, chapters, events, custom prompts, entity accounts OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\") embedder Embedder embed , search , chapter boundaries, entity linking OpenAIEmbedder(\"text-embedding-3-small\") An unset role uses its default. VLM and LLM are separate, so they can be different models."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Models",
"url": "pages/models.html#models",
"text": "Models(vlm=None, llm=None, embedder=None) from vidra import Anthropic, LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI models = Models(vlm=OpenAI(\"gpt-5.4-mini\"), llm=Anthropic(\"claude-haiku-4-5\"), embedder=LocalEmbedder()) video_rag(\"shop.mp4\", \"data/out\", models=models) # uses vlm and embedder aggregates.aggregate(out=..., models=models, summary=...) # uses llm and embedder search(\"a customer paying\", \"shop\", models=models) # uses embedder Build once and pass everywhere, so indexing and search use the same embedder. Models are checked at construction: right class, a key , and the model's own problems() (e.g. a missing API key). Functions also take vlm= , llm= , embedder= ; giving a role both ways is refused. models.resolved() shows each role with defaults filled in."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Ready-made models",
"url": "pages/models.html#ready-made",
"text": "Class Roles Talks to OpenAI VLM, LLM OpenAI's Responses API Anthropic VLM, LLM Anthropic's Messages API Chat VLM, LLM any server speaking OpenAI's Chat Completions API Stub VLM, LLM nothing: placeholder answers in the right shape, for tests OpenAIEmbedder embedder OpenAI, or any server with an /embeddings endpoint LocalEmbedder embedder a sentence-transformers model in this process HashEmbedder embedder nothing: vectors from word hashes, for tests The VLM/LLM classes fill either role."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "OpenAI",
"url": "pages/models.html#openai",
"text": "OpenAI(model=\"gpt-5.4-mini\", api_key=None, base_url=None, concurrency=8, client=None) Argument Meaning model The model id. Its key is openai:<model> . api_key Default: OPENAI_API_KEY . base_url Another endpoint for the same API, e.g. a proxy. concurrency Calls in flight at once. client A ready openai.AsyncOpenAI ."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Anthropic",
"url": "pages/models.html#anthropic",
"text": "Anthropic(model=\"claude-haiku-4-5\", api_key=None, base_url=\"https://api.anthropic.com\", concurrency=8, client=None) As OpenAI , but client is an httpx.AsyncClient , the key defaults to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY , and the model key is anthropic:<model> . Retries rate limits and server errors twice. Tested against a mock server only."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Chat",
"url": "pages/models.html#chat",
"text": "Chat(model, base_url, name=\"chat\", api_key=None, structured=\"json_schema\", token_field=\"max_tokens\", concurrency=8, client=None) Any server with OpenAI's Chat Completions API. Run against OpenAI's endpoint; other servers tested against a mock only. Argument Meaning model The model id the server knows. base_url The API root, usually ending in /v1 . name First part of the key ( <name>:<model> ), to tell servers apart. api_key Optional for local servers. structured How structure is enforced: \"json_schema\" (by the server), \"json_object\" (any JSON), or \"prompt\" (schema in the prompt). Use a weaker mode if the server rejects JSON Schema. token_field The output-cap parameter, max_tokens or max_completion_tokens ; retried with the other if refused. concurrency Calls in flight; 1 for single-request servers. client A ready openai.AsyncOpenAI . import os from vidra import Chat vlm = Chat(\"gpt-5.4-mini\", base_url=\"https://api.openai.com/v1\", name=\"openai-chat\", api_key=os.environ[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"])"
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Stub",
"url": "pages/models.html#stub",
"text": "Stub() returns placeholder answers in the requested shape, instantly. Key: stub . For running without a key."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "OpenAIEmbedder",
"url": "pages/models.html#openai-embedder",
"text": "OpenAIEmbedder(model=\"text-embedding-3-small\", api_key=None, base_url=None, name=\"openai\", dims=None, input_type=False, query_prefix=None, document_prefix=None, client=None) Argument Meaning model The embedding model. api_key Default OPENAI_API_KEY ; optional with base_url . base_url Another server with an OpenAI-style /embeddings . name The first part of the key: openai:text-embedding-3-small:1536 . dims Requested width (sent as dimensions ). input_type Send query / document with each call (e.g. Voyage). query_prefix , document_prefix Text before each query or passage. Known models get theirs automatically; setting one changes the key. client A ready openai.OpenAI . The width is part of the key. OpenAI widths are known; other models are probed once per process."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "LocalEmbedder",
"url": "pages/models.html#local-embedder",
"text": "LocalEmbedder(model=\"BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5\", dims=None, device=None, batch=32, query_prefix=None, document_prefix=None) Argument Meaning model A sentence-transformers model on Hugging Face, downloaded on first use. dims Expected width; checked. device Default: cuda, then mps, then the CPU. batch Texts per forward pass. query_prefix , document_prefix As for OpenAIEmbedder ; e5, nomic, bge and mxbai get theirs automatically. Needs vidra[local] . Key: local:<model>:<width> . The default matched text-embedding-3-small on our retrieval tests, at 0.05 s per query vs 0.6 s."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "HashEmbedder",
"url": "pages/models.html#hash-embedder",
"text": "HashEmbedder(dims=256) hashes words into vectors: no model, no network. Exact words only, so for tests. Key: hash:none:<dims> ."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Writing your own",
"url": "pages/models.html#own",
"text": "Subclass a base, set key , fill in one method ( async def or plain def ). from vidra import Embedder, LLM, VLM class MyVLM(VLM): key = \"mylab:vision-v2\" async def generate(self, parts, schema=None, system=None, max_output_tokens=4000): ... return {\"summary\": \"...\", \"setting\": \"...\"} # a dict, or its JSON text class MyLLM(LLM): key = \"mylab:text-v1\" def complete(self, prompt, schema=None, system=None, max_output_tokens=4000): ... return \"...\" # text, or a dict for a schema class MyEmbedder(Embedder): key = \"mylab:embed-v1:768\" def embed(self, texts): ... return [[0.0] * 768 for _ in texts] # one vector per text, one width"
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "VLM.generate",
"url": "pages/models.html#vlm-method",
"text": "generate(parts, schema=None, system=None, max_output_tokens=4000) Argument Is parts The request in order: the instruction, then a label and image per frame. Each part is {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": str} or {\"type\": \"image\", \"data\": bytes, \"mime\": \"image/jpeg\"} . schema {\"name\": str, \"schema\": dict} , a strict JSON Schema to match, or None for prose. system The system prompt, or None . max_output_tokens Answer length cap. Return a dict matching the schema, or a JSON string. Without a schema, return text."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "LLM.complete",
"url": "pages/models.html#llm-method",
"text": "complete(prompt, schema=None, system=None, max_output_tokens=4000) prompt is a string; otherwise as generate ."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Embedder.embed and embed_query",
"url": "pages/models.html#embedder-method",
"text": "embed(texts) -> list[list[float]] embed_query(text) -> list[float] embed(texts) returns one vector per text, all one width. embed_query(text) embeds search queries; it defaults to embed([text])[0] ."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Attributes and checks",
"url": "pages/models.html#attributes",
"text": "Member Meaning key Required identity ( below ). May be a lazy property. concurrency Calls in flight at once. Default 8. problems() Reasons it can't run (e.g. no key), checked before work; the first raises ModelUnavailable . name , model The parts of key before and after the first colon. Read-only: keep your own client or weights under another attribute ( self.client , self.encoder )."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Keys",
"url": "pages/models.html#keys",
"text": "The key is stored with every answer and vector and decides reuse: Change it when the model changes , or old answers are reused. For an embedder it names the vector space; include the width ( mylab:embed-v1:768 ). Keep it stable for the same model, or everything is recomputed."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "What the library does around your method",
"url": "pages/models.html#calls",
"text": "At most concurrency calls run at once per instance. A plain def runs in a thread. JSON strings are parsed when a schema was asked; non-object answers are refused. Exceptions become ModelFailed , naming the key. Retry inside the method if needed."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Errors",
"url": "pages/models.html#errors",
"text": "Class Raised when Refused a model is the wrong class for its role ( vlm must be a VLM, not MyLLM ) or has no key vidra.ModelUnavailable a model reports a problem (no key) before work, or a local model won't load ModelFailed a call failed: refusal, network error, wrong shape ( vidra.shared.models.base.ModelFailed ) All three are VidraError s; the last two are vidra.Unavailable ."
},
{
"page": "Models",
"title": "Complete example",
"url": "pages/models.html#example",
"text": "A VLM and LLM calling the OpenAI SDK directly, and an embedder using sentence-transformers. docs/pages/examples/custom_models.py \"\"\"Models of your own: subclass VLM, LLM or Embedder and fill in one method. These three wrap the OpenAI SDK and sentence-transformers directly, to show what a method receives and must return; any other client works the same way. python custom_models.py path/to/video.mp4 \"\"\" import base64 import os import sys import vidra from vidra import LLM, VLM, Embedder, Folder, Models, aggregates from vidra.video_rag import search, video_rag vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") def json_format(schema): \"\"\"`schema` is {\"name\": ..., \"schema\": <JSON Schema>}, or None for prose.\"\"\" if schema is None: return {} return {\"response_format\": {\"type\": \"json_schema\", \"json_schema\": {**schema, \"strict\": True}}} class MyVLM(VLM): \"\"\"Describes frames. `generate` may be async, as here, or a plain def.\"\"\" key = \"mine:gpt-5.4-mini\" # the identity stored with every answer concurrency = 4 # calls in flight at once def __init__(self): from openai import AsyncOpenAI self.client = AsyncOpenAI() def problems(self): # Checked before any work starts, so a missing key fails at once. return [] if os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\") else [\"OPENAI_API_KEY is not set\"] async def generate(self, parts, schema=None, system=None, max_output_tokens=4000): # parts: {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": ...} and # {\"type\": \"image\", \"data\": <bytes>, \"mime\": \"image/jpeg\"}, in order. content = [] for part in parts: if part[\"type\"] == \"text\": content.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": part[\"text\"]}) else: data = base64.b64encode(part[\"data\"]).decode() content.append({\"type\": \"image_url\", \"image_url\": {\"url\": f\"data:{part['mime']};base64,{data}\"}}) messages = ([{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system}] if system else []) messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": content}) response = await self.client.chat.completions.create( model=\"gpt-5.4-mini\", messages=messages, max_completion_tokens=max_output_tokens, **json_format(schema)) return response.choices[0].message.content # JSON text is parsed for you class MyLLM(LLM): \"\"\"Writes summaries, chapters, events and entity accounts. A plain def runs in a thread.\"\"\" key = \"mine:gpt-5.4-mini\" def __init__(self): from openai import OpenAI self.client = OpenAI() def complete(self, prompt, schema=None, system=None, max_output_tokens=4000): messages = ([{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system}] if system else []) messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}) response = self.client.chat.completions.create( model=\"gpt-5.4-mini\", messages=messages, max_completion_tokens=max_output_tokens, **json_format(schema)) return response.choices[0].message.content class MyEmbedder(Embedder): \"\"\"Text to vectors. The key names the vector space: include the width.\"\"\" key = \"mine:all-MiniLM-L6-v2:384\" def __init__(self): from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer self.encoder = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\") def embed(self, texts): return self.encoder.encode(list(texts), normalize_embeddings=True).tolist() # Override embed_query only when a query is embedded differently. models = Models(vlm=MyVLM(), llm=MyLLM(), embedder=MyEmbedder()) database = Folder(\"data/out\") run = video_rag(sys.argv[1], \"data/out\", sampler=\"clip\", use_audio=False, models=models, database=database) moments, _ = search(\"people at a counter\", run.video_id, models=models, database=database) print([(m.chunk_id, round(m.start_ts, 1)) for m in moments]) d = run.folder video = aggregates.record(timeline=d / \"timeline.json\", descriptions=d / \"descriptions.json\") aggregates.summary(input=video.excerpt(answers={\"clip\": [\"summary\"]}), out=d / \"answers\" / \"summary.json\", models=models) print(aggregates.load(d / \"answers\" / \"summary.json\").stats[\"model\"]) # mine:gpt-5.4-mini"
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "Databases",
"url": "pages/databases.html",
"text": "Where runs copy their output and searches read from: Supabase, a folder, or your own class."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "Choosing one",
"url": "pages/databases.html#choose",
"text": "Database Keeps Search Needs Supabase() every artifact and answer, as Postgres rows hybrid: vectors and full text, fused a Supabase project with the schema installed Folder(root) nothing; reads the output folder in place vectors only nothing your own Database subclass whatever its hooks keep whatever its read hooks do your code Pass it as database= to video_rag , workflow , aggregates.aggregate , search and aggregates.search , or by name ( \"supabase\" , \"folder\" ). Build once and reuse. A Database is a context manager that calls close() on exit."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "Supabase",
"url": "pages/databases.html#supabase",
"text": "Supabase(url=None, key=None, read_key=None) Argument Default Meaning url SUPABASE_URL The project URL. key SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY Secret key, for writes. read_key SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY Publishable key, for searches. Connects on first use. Setup, once per project: In the SQL editor, run db/supabase/video_rag.sql , then db/supabase/aggregates.sql . This creates the vidra schema: vr_ tables for moments, ag_ tables for aggregates, and the search functions. Add vidra under Settings → API → Exposed schemas . Otherwise requests fail with PGRST106 . Put the URL and keys in .env , or pass them in code. Search fuses vector similarity and Postgres full-text search. Re-cutting a grid never deletes descriptions, embeddings or answers. db/supabase/reset.sql drops everything; db/wipe.py deletes videos locally and in Supabase."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "Folder",
"url": "pages/databases.html#folder",
"text": "Folder(root=None) Searches <root>/<video_id>/ in place, by cosine similarity. root defaults to the data root's out/ . Point it at the run's output folder and nothing is copied: db = Folder(\"data/out\") run = video_rag(\"shop.mp4\", \"data/out\", models=models, database=db) search(\"a customer paying\", run.video_id, models=models, database=db) Aggregate vectors are kept in aggregate_units.json in the source's folder. Suits one machine and a few hundred videos; no full-text search, so exact names and numbers rank worse than on Supabase."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "Writing your own",
"url": "pages/databases.html#own",
"text": "Subclass Database and fill in only the hooks you need: Unfilled write hooks do nothing ; that artifact isn't read or copied. Unfilled read hooks raise Unsupported (an Unavailable and NotImplementedError ). from vidra import Database class VectorsOnly(Database): name = \"vectors\" def write_embedded(self, video_id, document): for unit in document[\"units\"]: my_index.upsert(id=f\"{video_id}/{unit['chunk_id']}/{unit['sampler_id']}\", vector=unit[\"vector\"], metadata={**unit, \"video_id\": video_id, \"embedder\": document[\"embedder\"]}) video_rag(\"shop.mp4\", \"data/out\", database=VectorsOnly(), models=models) name labels your database in run.problems . A hook that raises is recorded in run.problems (or stats[\"problems\"] for aggregates) and the run continues. db.implements(\"write_embedded\") says whether a hook is filled in."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "When each hook is called",
"url": "pages/databases.html#when",
"text": "video_rag , workflow : after each stage, write_<artifact>(video_id, document) per file written, with its JSON as a dict. After describe , also write_prompts(rows) . aggregates.aggregate(database=...) , workflow : write_source once (if it fails, nothing else runs), write_answer per answer, write_definitions once, then write_aggregate_units once, only if implemented, since it costs an embedding call. search : video_ids() when no video is named, spans(video_id) per video (unless grids= ), then search(...) . aggregates.search : search_aggregates(...) . video_rag_live : write_media when the stream opens (no duration yet); write_observations(video_id, rows) as answers arrive, through one writer (immediately when it keeps up, the backlog in one call when it does not); then the batch documents when the stream ends. search_observations : search_observations(...) ."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "video_rag write hooks",
"url": "pages/databases.html#write-hooks",
"text": "Each receives the video id and the document as its JSON file holds it (fields: Reference ). Hook Receives write_media(video_id, document) media.json : path , container_format , duration_s , video and audio streams, source (a fingerprint of the file), name , recorded_at write_raw_transcript(video_id, document) transcript.raw.json : segments , words and turns with times and speakers, speakers , model , track , stats write_cuts(video_id, document) cuts.json : cuts (times), scores , source , detector , params , stats write_timeline(video_id, document) timeline.json : chunks (each chunk_id , start_ts , end_ts ), policy , params , fingerprint , duration_s , chunk_count write_manifest(video_id, document) manifest.json : chunks (each with samplers : {sampler: {frame_count, frames}} ), source , config , stats write_transcript(video_id, document) transcript.json : chunks (each chunk_id , text , word_count , turns , structured.speakers ) write_descriptions(video_id, document) descriptions.json : chunks (each with samplers : {answer_id: {sampler, question, description, structured, frame_indexes, ...}} ), model write_embedded(video_id, document) embedded.json : embedder (the key) and units , each with chunk_id , sampler_id , sampler , question , content , structured , text_hash , vector write_prompts(rows) the questions a describe run asked: each name , version (the hash stored with its answers), instruction , shape , summary , builtin , about write_observations(video_id, rows) a live run 's answers, called many times per run: each row one kept frame and question, with chunk_id , sampler_id , sampler , question , frame_index , media_ts , frames , description , structured , content , text_hash , seen_at , answered_at , lag_s , gap_before , embedder , vector . Key a row by (video_id, sampler_id, frame_index, embedder) . Search needs at least write_timeline and write_embedded (or grids= on search instead of the timeline)."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "aggregates write hooks",
"url": "pages/databases.html#aggregate-hooks",
"text": "A source is what answers are about: one video, or several combined . source_id is the record's video id. Hook Receives write_source(source) source_id , video_ids , members (each video_id , first_chunk , chunk_count , offset_s : where it sits on the combined clock), duration_s , chunk_count write_answer(source_id, answer, items, mentions) answer : aggregate_id , aggregator , tier , payload (whole), inputs , model , version , inputs_fingerprint . items : what the answer places in time (a chapter, an event, a name ner found, a linked entity), each item_id , item_kind , label , text , chunk_ids , start_ts , end_ts , data . mentions : for a linked entity, each sighting: item_id , mention_key , chunk_id , sampler_id , entry , doubt . Empty otherwise. write_definitions(rows) each prompt or profile used: name , version , kind , definition (the entry as stored), builtin write_aggregate_units(source_id, units, embedder_key) the embedded summary, chapters and entity accounts, each aggregate_id , item_id (empty for a summary), level ( source , span or entity ), content , start_ts , end_ts , text_hash , vector . Defining this hook is what makes a run embed them. Re-runs resend every answer, reused ones too: replace what you hold for that source_id and aggregate_id ."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "Read hooks",
"url": "pages/databases.html#read-hooks",
"text": "Needed only for search."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "video_ids()",
"url": "pages/databases.html#hook-video-ids",
"text": "Every video id held, as a list. Used when a search names no video."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "spans(video_id)",
"url": "pages/databases.html#hook-spans",
"text": "The grid: [(start_ts, end_ts), ...] in chunk order (index = chunk id). Gives moments their times and resolves after / before ."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "search(...)",
"url": "pages/databases.html#hook-search",
"text": "search(vector, query, embedder_key, limit=20, video_ids=None, sampler=None, question=None, strategy=None, chunk_ids=None, structured=None) -> list[dict] Argument Is vector The query's vector. query The query's text, for full-text search. embedder_key Only compare units with this embedder . limit Units to return (the search's candidates ). video_ids Only these videos; None is all. sampler Only units whose sampler_id equals this. question Only units whose question equals this. strategy Only units whose sampler equals this. chunk_ids Only these chunks (time windows already resolved). structured Only units whose fields equal each value, or whose list contains it. Return units best first, as dicts with video_id , chunk_id , sampler_id , sampler , question , content , structured , score , dense_rank (1 = best) and text_rank (or None ). Only the order matters."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "search_aggregates(...)",
"url": "pages/databases.html#hook-search-aggregates",
"text": "search_aggregates(vector, query, embedder_key, level, limit=5, source_ids=None) -> list[dict] Rank one level 's units under embedder_key , optionally only source_ids . Return dicts with source_id , video_ids , aggregate_id , item_id , level , content , start_ts , end_ts , score , best first."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "search_observations(...)",
"url": "pages/databases.html#hook-search-observations",
"text": "search_observations(vector, query, embedder_key, limit=20, video_ids=None, sampler=None, question=None, strategy=None, after=None, before=None, since=None, until=None, structured=None) -> list[dict] Rank a live run's rows under embedder_key . The filters are those of search , plus after / before on media_ts and since / until on seen_at (ISO 8601 UTC strings). Return dicts with video_id , chunk_id , sampler_id , sampler , question , frame_index , media_ts , frames , description , structured , seen_at , score , dense_rank , text_rank , best first."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "close()",
"url": "pages/databases.html#hook-close",
"text": "Release connections. Called by with ; safe to call twice."
},
{
"page": "Databases",
"title": "Complete example: SQLite",
"url": "pages/databases.html#example",
"text": "Grid, moment vectors and aggregate vectors in one SQLite file, searched by cosine similarity. docs/pages/examples/custom_database.py \"\"\"A database of your own: SQLite, holding the grid, the moment vectors and the aggregate vectors, and searching both. Fill in only the hooks you need. A write hook left out does nothing (that artifact is not copied); a read hook left out raises `Unsupported`. python custom_database.py path/to/video.mp4 \"\"\" import json import math import sqlite3 import sys import vidra from vidra import Database, LocalEmbedder, Models, OpenAI, aggregates from vidra.video_rag import search, video_rag vidra.configure(env_file=\".env\") def cosine(a, b): dot = sum(x * y for x, y in zip(a, b)) return dot / ((math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in a)) * math.sqrt(sum(y * y for y in b))) or 1.0) def matches(fields, wanted): \"\"\"Every wanted field equal to its value, or a list holding it.\"\"\" return all(fields.get(k) == v or (isinstance(fields.get(k), list) and v in fields[k]) for k, v in wanted.items()) class SQLite(Database): name = \"sqlite\" # what run.problems calls it def __init__(self, path=\"vidra.sqlite\"): self.db = sqlite3.connect(path) self.db.executescript(\"\"\" create table if not exists chunks (video_id text, chunk_id int, start_ts real, end_ts real, primary key (video_id, chunk_id)); create table if not exists units (video_id text, chunk_id int, sampler_id text, sampler text, question text, content text, structured text, embedder text, vector text, primary key (video_id, chunk_id, sampler_id, embedder)); create table if not exists sources (source_id text primary key, video_ids text); create table if not exists aggregate_units (source_id text, aggregate_id text, item_id text, level text, content text, start_ts real, end_ts real, embedder text, vector text); \"\"\") # ---- writes: called as each stage finishes, with the file's JSON as a dict def write_timeline(self, video_id, document): self.db.execute(\"delete from chunks where video_id = ?\", (video_id,)) self.db.executemany(\"insert into chunks values (?, ?, ?, ?)\", [(video_id, c[\"chunk_id\"], c[\"start_ts\"], c[\"end_ts\"]) for c in document[\"chunks\"]]) self.db.commit() def write_embedded(self, video_id, document): self.db.executemany( \"insert or replace into units values (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\", [(video_id, u[\"chunk_id\"], u[\"sampler_id\"], u[\"sampler\"], u[\"question\"], u[\"content\"], json.dumps(u[\"structured\"]), document[\"embedder\"], json.dumps(u[\"vector\"])) for u in document[\"units\"] if u.get(\"vector\")]) self.db.commit() def write_source(self, source): self.db.execute(\"insert or replace into sources values (?, ?)\", (source[\"source_id\"], json.dumps(source[\"video_ids\"]))) self.db.commit() def write_aggregate_units(self, source_id, units, embedder_key): # Defining this hook is what makes a run embed summaries and chapters. ids = {u[\"aggregate_id\"] for u in units} self.db.executemany(\"delete from aggregate_units where source_id = ? \" \"and aggregate_id = ?\", [(source_id, a) for a in ids]) self.db.executemany( \"insert into aggregate_units values (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\", [(source_id, u[\"aggregate_id\"], u[\"item_id\"], u[\"level\"], u[\"content\"], u.get(\"start_ts\"), u.get(\"end_ts\"), embedder_key, json.dumps(u[\"vector\"])) for u in units]) self.db.commit() # ---- reads: needed only to search through this database def video_ids(self): return [row[0] for row in self.db.execute(\"select distinct video_id from chunks\")] def spans(self, video_id): return [(start, end) for start, end in self.db.execute( \"select start_ts, end_ts from chunks where video_id = ? order by chunk_id\", (video_id,))] def search(self, vector, query, embedder_key, limit=20, video_ids=None, sampler=None, question=None, strategy=None, chunk_ids=None, structured=None): rows = [] for (vid, chunk, sampler_id, sampler_name, asked, content, fields, vec) in self.db.execute( \"select video_id, chunk_id, sampler_id, sampler, question, content, \" \"structured, vector from units where embedder = ?\", (embedder_key,)): fields = json.loads"
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "Reference",
"url": "pages/reference.html",
"text": "File formats, errors, storage locations and hardware."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "Documents",
"url": "pages/reference.html#documents",
"text": "Every document is a JSON object with document (its kind), version and video_id , and is what the matching write_<artifact> hook receives. Times are in seconds. Each stage's load reads one back, typed."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "media.json",
"url": "pages/reference.html#doc-media",
"text": "Field Is path The file's path when read. container_format Container format. duration_s The container's duration. video The picture stream, or null : index , codec , rate (frames per second), time_base , width , height , frames , duration_s . audio The soundtrack, or null : index , codec , rate (samples per second), channels , duration_s . source Content fingerprint, distinguishing a moved file from a different one. name Display name; the filename unless given. recorded_at Recording time (ISO 8601) from tags unless given, or null ."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "transcript.raw.json",
"url": "pages/reference.html#doc-raw-transcript",
"text": "Field Is segments Whisper's utterances: start , end , text , speaker . words Each word: start , end , text , speaker . turns Diarization's turns: speaker , start , end . speakers The speaker labels, e.g. [\"SPEAKER_00\"] . model Transcriber, diarizer, settings, detected language. track The decoded audio: rate , duration_s , samples , rms , peak , silent . stats Counts (segments, words, speakers, turns, speech seconds) and timings."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "cuts.json",
"url": "pages/reference.html#doc-cuts",
"text": "Field Is cuts The boundary times. source video or audio . detector content for the scene detector, or the policy name. params Settings used ( threshold , stride , ...). scores Per-frame scores ( metric , stride , at , values ) for retune and calibrate , or null . stats Frames read and scored, timing, cuts found."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "timeline.json",
"url": "pages/reference.html#doc-timeline",
"text": "Field Is chunks The grid: chunk_id , start_ts , end_ts , contiguous. policy uniform , scene , vad or speaker . derived_from video , audio , grid (arithmetic), or combined . params Settings used ( min_s , max_s , ...); for a combination, combined places each video. fingerprint Grid hash, recorded by every later document to detect mismatched grids. duration_s , chunk_count The grid's length and size."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "manifest.json",
"url": "pages/reference.html#doc-manifest",
"text": "Field Is chunks Per chunk: chunk_id , decimated_frames (frames offered), and samplers : {sampler_id: {frame_count, frames}} , each frame with index (its file in the store), media_ts , chunk_local_index , pts . source What was decoded: path, container, duration, stream properties. video.recreate checks against it. config Decimator, sampler settings (with prompts ) and frame store settings. stats frames_decimated , frames_sampled (picks), stored_frames (files), stored_mb , timing. timeline_fingerprint , manifest_fingerprint Grid hash, and a hash of this sampling."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "transcript.json",
"url": "pages/reference.html#doc-transcript",
"text": "Field Is chunks Per chunk, silent ones included: chunk_id , text , word_count , turns ( speaker , start , end , text ), structured ( {\"speakers\": [...]} ). model Carried from the raw transcript. stats Chunks, chunks with speech, words, words outside the grid, speakers. timeline_fingerprint The grid it was cut on."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "descriptions.json",
"url": "pages/reference.html#doc-descriptions",
"text": "Field Is chunks Per chunk: chunk_id and samplers : {answer_id: answer} . Each answer has sampler , question , description (the prose), structured (the fields), frame_count , frame_indexes , elapsed_s . model The VLM: name , params and prompts ( {question: hash} ); compared for reuse. stats Described, skipped (reused), chunks, timing. timeline_fingerprint , manifest_fingerprint The grid and sampling described."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "embedded.json",
"url": "pages/reference.html#doc-embedded",
"text": "Field Is embedder The embedder's key: the vector space. units Each unit: chunk_id , sampler_id (answer id or transcript ), sampler , question , content , structured , text_hash , characters , vector . count , samplers How many units, and which answer ids. timeline_fingerprint The grid."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "Aggregate answers",
"url": "pages/reference.html#doc-answer",
"text": "One file per answer, named by its id ( summary.json ; entities:people as entities.people.json ): Field Is aggregate_id summary , entities:people , or with a label sentiment~spoken . tier free , local or llm . payload The answer; keys per aggregator on Aggregates . inputs_fingerprint A hash of the text it read. stats about , model (key), inputs , version (definition hash), read_chars . Saved inputs: an excerpt holds selection , the timeline , the rows (one per chunk with text) and the answers that contributed; a sightings file holds the profile , selection , field_name , identity keys , the timeline , the mentions (each chunk_id , sampler_id , field , index , signature , entry ) and, when the profile reads it, the transcript of the chunks mentioned."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "Receipts: Produced",
"url": "pages/reference.html#produced",
"text": "Returned by every stage and aggregator: Field Is video_id The video id used ( media may mint a new one). component Which stage or aggregator. artifacts {name: path} of what was written. stats Its headline numbers. skipped What didn't run, e.g. [\"evidence\"] under uniform . JSON Schemas are in db/json/ ; python -m vidra.shared.contracts.schemas --check checks them."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "Errors",
"url": "pages/reference.html#errors",
"text": "Every deliberate error is a vidra.VidraError with a builtin base, so except ValueError etc. still work. Class Also a Raised when vidra.VidraError the base of everything below vidra.Unavailable this setup cannot do it: no package, weights, key or server. Retrying will not help vidra.ModelUnavailable Unavailable a model reports a problem (no API key), or a local model will not load ModelFailed Unavailable a model call failed ( vidra.shared.models.base ) Refused ValueError the request is invalid as given ( vidra.shared.reporting.errors ) UnknownOption ValueError , KeyError a value outside a fixed set: an unknown policy, sampler, backend MissingArtifact FileNotFoundError a stage's input file does not exist; the message names the stage that writes it. Also a search with nothing indexed UnusableVideoId ValueError a video id with characters a folder name cannot safely have Unsupported Unavailable, NotImplementedError a database does not implement a read hook ( vidra.shared.storage.database ) SchemaOutOfDate Unavailable the Supabase schema is older than the code: re-run the SQL files media.UnusableMedia RuntimeError the file cannot be opened, or has neither video nor audio media.VideoIdTaken FileExistsError another file holds the id and on_conflict=\"refuse\" video.UnreadableSource RuntimeError no readable video stream video.Mismatch ValueError recreate : the video is not the one the manifest was built from video.MissingVideo FileNotFoundError recreate : no file at video describe.DescriberUnavailable Unavailable the vision model cannot be reached describe.StoreUnavailable Unavailable the frame store, or a frame it should hold, is missing describe.PromptError ValueError a question is invalid or unknown describe.ProtectedPrompt PromptError a built-in question cannot be changed embed.EmbedderUnavailable Unavailable the embedder cannot be reached or loaded aggregates.RecordError ValueError a record cannot be opened, or an input asks for what it lacks aggregates.AggregateError ValueError an unknown aggregator, or the wrong kind of input aggregates.Inapplicable ValueError nothing to answer; the pipeline skips it with the reason aggregates.DefinitionError ValueError a prompt or profile is invalid or unknown aggregates.ProtectedDefinition DefinitionError a built-in prompt or profile cannot be changed CombineError ValueError combine cannot lay these records end to end (one named twice) import vidra try: run = video_rag(\"shop.mp4\", \"data/out\", models=models) except vidra.Unavailable as missing: # install or configure something print(\"cannot run here:\", missing) except vidra.VidraError as refused: # the request itself print(\"refused:\", refused)"
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "Where things are kept",
"url": "pages/reference.html#configuration",
"text": "What Where Change with Output (default for workflow and Folder ) <data root>/out/ configure(data_root=) , VIDRA_DATA Custom questions <data root>/prompts.json the same Custom prompts and profiles <data root>/aggregates.json the same Detector and embedder checkpoints weights/ configure(weights=) , VIDRA_WEIGHTS CLIP, pyannote, GLiNER, DistilBERT Hugging Face's cache HF_HOME The data root is data/ in a checkout, else ~/.vidra . Precedence: configure() , environment variables, defaults. VIDRA_DATA and VIDRA_WEIGHTS are not read from .env . Folders starting with _ are never listed as videos. Logs go to the vidra logger, with no handlers configured. logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO) shows each stage; failed database writes are warnings."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "Hardware",
"url": "pages/reference.html#hardware",
"text": "PyTorch models (CLIP, YOLO, local embedder, pyannote) use CUDA, then mps , then CPU. Whisper uses CUDA or CPU. GLiNER and sentiment run on the CPU. RTX 4060 laptop: Work GPU CPU Whisper small + pyannote, 205 s of narration 21 s 316 s clip , yolo and objects , 60 s video 25 s 52 s text , 60 s of slides 13 s 212 s describe, 18 calls of 6 frames, gpt-5.4-mini 13 s at concurrency 8; 76 s one at a time mps is untested. If pyannote fails on a Mac, set PYTORCH_ENABLE_MPS_FALLBACK=1 before starting Python. Intel Macs can't install the required PyTorch. Whisper on an NVIDIA GPU needs CUDA 12's cuBLAS and cuDNN (installed by vidra[audio] ); without them it is refused before the run, or use device=\"cpu\" . Decoding 3 hours of 720p at one frame per second takes about 2 minutes."
},
{
"page": "Reference",
"title": "Checking an install",
"url": "pages/reference.html#checks",
"text": "python -m vidra.shared.contracts.schemas --check : schemas match the document types. video.recreate(..., verify=store) : rebuilds frames and compares them byte for byte ( recreate ). python docs/pages/build.py --check : docs cover every public function and parameter. --run a.mp4 b.mp4 runs every example with free stand-in models."
}
